{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012KuW86r7xRdkruZQwN1yp3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'IRT person-fit provides a principled contamination detection\n2\t  framework at the minimal-information operating point, with unique mechanistic interpretability\n3\t  (θ-shift analysis, memorization fraction quantification, parametric null distribution).\n4\t  While simpler statistics (HT) achieve comparable raw detection power, lz* offers:\n5\t  (i) calibrated hypothesis testing via known null N(0,1), (ii) Snijders correction\n6\t  for θ estimation error, (iii) full 4PL item-heterogeneity weighting critical for\n7\t  multi-domain benchmarks like MMLU. Post-RL robustness is demonstrated but shared\n8\t  across the person-fit family — the structural immunity to distributional shifts\n9\t  is a class-level advantage over log-prob methods. Claims soften from ''lz* uniquely\n10\t  robust'' to ''person-fit family robust; lz* uniquely interpretable.''\n11\t\n12\t  '\n13\timagined_experiments:\n14\t- name: Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen)\n15\t  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam-pilot\n16\t  description: 'Qwen3.5-9B × 4 conditions (0%-seed1/0%-seed2/15%/50%) × MMLU only.\n17\t    Go/no-go 信号实验。\n18\t\n19\t    '\n20\t  expected_results:\n21\t    clean_seed1_lz_star: 8.5\n22\t    clean_seed2_lz_star: 7.9\n23\t    clean_mean: 8.2\n24\t    clean_std: 0.42\n25\t    contam_15_lz_star: 4.1\n26\t    contam_50_lz_star: 7.0\n27\t    delta_lz_star_15: -4.1\n28\t    delta_lz_star_50: -1.2\n29\t    cohens_d_contam15: -3.2\n30\t    cohens_d_contam50: -1.1\n31\t    contam_15_acc: 0.72\n32\t    contam_50_acc: 0.76\n33\t    memorization_fraction_15: 0.36\n34\t    memorization_fraction_50: 0.28\n35\t    seen_lz_star_15: 0.3\n36\t    unseen_lz_star_15: 3.2\n37\t    theta_shift_15: 0.25\n38\t    theta_shift_50: 0.45\n39\t    theta_fixed_contam15_lz: 11.5\n40\t    theta_fixed_contam50_lz: 17.8\n41\t    theta_fixed_ratio: 2.9\n42\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 Qwen 控制实验预期产生强效应但 free-θ 下 50% contamination 出现 non-monotonicity。Qwen\n43\t    baseline lz* 高 (~8-9) 因其 response pattern 与 4PL 预测高度一致但非完美匹配；15% 污染产生明显 aberrance（memorization\n44\t    fraction ~36% 意味着约 1/3 seen items 被记忆，产生 difficulty-inconsistent correct responses）。\n45\t    50% 条件下 θ-shift 吸收大量 aberrance 信号导致 free-θ d 值下降至 ~1.1，但 θ-fixed 恢复单调性（ratio ~2.9）。这与\n46\t    Qwen 高 baseline misfit (lz*~8.5) 交互——高 baseline 模型更容易出现 non-monotonicity 因为 θ\n47\t    估计对 response pattern 变化更敏感。\n48\t\n49\t    '\n50\t  tables:\n51\t  - name: 'Table: Qwen Pilot Controlled Contamination Results'\n52\t    columns:\n53\t    - condition\n54\t    - lz_star\n55\t    - delta_lz_star\n56\t    - cohens_d\n57\t    - acc\n58\t    - theta_mle\n59\t    - lz_star_fixed\n60\t    - memo_frac\n61\t    rows:\n62\t    - - clean_s1\n63\t      - 8.5\n64\t      - 0\n65\t      - '-'\n66\t      - 0.678\n67\t      - -0.1\n68\t      - '-'\n69\t      - '-'\n70\t    - - clean_s2\n71\t      - 7.9\n72\t      - 0\n73\t      - '-'\n74\t      - 0.676\n75\t      - -0.11\n76\t      - '-'\n77\t      - '-'\n78\t    - - contam_15\n79\t      - 4.1\n80\t      - -4.1\n81\t      - -3.2\n82\t      - 0.72\n83\t      - 0.15\n84\t      - 11.5\n85\t      - 0.36\n86\t    - - contam_50\n87\t      - 7.0\n88\t      - -1.2\n89\t      - -1.1\n90\t      - 0.76\n91\t      - 0.35\n92\t      - 17.8\n93\t      - 0.28\n94\t  figures_description:\n95\t  - 'Bar chart: clean vs contam_15 vs contam_50 lz* (free-θ vs θ-fixed)'\n96\t  - 'Scatter: seen vs unseen item lz* contribution at 15% contamination'\n97\t  analysis: 'Go 信号确认。|d|>2 at 15% 足以支撑 Claim 1。Non-monotonicity 在 free-θ 下出现 是预期的，θ-fixed\n98\t    恢复单调性是方法论贡献。Memorization fraction ~36% 与 SFT generalization 一致——QLoRA 仅记忆约 1/3\n99\t    注入 items，其余通过泛化提升。\n100\t\n101\t    '\n102\t- name: Full Controlled Contamination (4 Families)\n103\t  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n104\t  description: 'Qwen3.5-9B + Gemma-4-31B + Llama-3.1-8B + Mistral-7B-v0.3 × 6 levels\n105\t    (0/5/10/15/25/50%) × MMLU + GSM8K + HellaSwag。\n106\t\n107\t    '\n108\t  expected_results:\n109\t    n_families_validated: 3\n110\t    qwen_mmlu_d15: -3.4\n111\t    qwen_mmlu_d50: -1.0\n112\t    llama_mmlu_d15: -2.9\n113\t    llama_mmlu_d50: -3.3\n114\t    mistral_mmlu_d15: -2.5\n115\t    mistral_mmlu_d50: -3.0\n116\t    gemma_mmlu_d15: -2.2\n117\t    gemma_mmlu_d50: -2.8\n118\t    gemma_note: Gemma 31B 参数量大，QLoRA 效率不同，可能需调参或 drop\n119\t    gsm8k_avg_d15: -1.5\n120\t    gsm8k_avg_d50: -2.0\n121\t    hellaswag_avg_d15: -1.8\n122\t    hellaswag_avg_d50: -2.5\n123\t    cross_family_memo_frac_range:\n124\t    - 0.3\n125\t    - 0.4\n126\t    cross_family_memo_frac_mean: 0.35\n127\t    dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed: true\n128\t    dose_response_monotonic_free: model-dependent\n129\t    n_conditions_total: 72\n130\t    n_conditions_significant: 55\n131\t    small_benchmark_weakness: GSM8K (1319 items) d ~1.5 at 15%, below MMLU\n132\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 3/4 families 成功验证（n_families_validated=3）。Gemma-4-31B\n133\t    因 参数量大且 QLoRA rank 可能不足，存在训练不稳定或效果弱化风险——median 档下 Gemma 可能仅提供 partial 结果或需 downgrade\n134\t    为 supporting evidence。跨 benchmark 差异反映 n_items 效应（MMLU 14042 >> GSM8K 1319）——power\n135\t    theory 预测 GSM8K 在 15% 仅有 ~59% power，对应 d ~1.5。HellaSwag (10042 items) 介于两者 之间。Memorization\n136\t    fraction 跨家族一致 (~35%) 是 SFT 机制的稳定性质， 不依赖模型架构——QLoRA 的泛化模式相似因为都是 low-rank adaptation。Free-θ\n137\t    non-monotonicity 仅出现在高 baseline lz* 模型（Qwen, Mistral），Llama (baseline ~0) 保持单调。\n138\t\n139\t    '\n140\t  tables:\n141\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Family Detection Summary (MMLU, θ-free)'\n142\t    columns:\n143\t    - family\n144\t    - clean_lz\n145\t    - d_5pct\n146\t    - d_10pct\n147\t    - d_15pct\n148\t    - d_25pct\n149\t    - d_50pct\n150\t    - memo_frac_15\n151\t    rows:\n152\t    - - Qwen-7B\n153\t      - 8.7\n154\t      - -0.8\n155\t      - -1.8\n156\t      - -3.4\n157\t      - -2.8\n158\t      - -1.0\n159\t      - 0.38\n160\t    - - Llama-8B\n161\t      - -0.1\n162\t      - -0.5\n163\t      - -1.5\n164\t      - -2.9\n165\t      - -3.1\n166\t      - -3.3\n167\t      - 0.35\n168\t    - - Mistral-7B\n169\t      - 5.4\n170\t      - -0.7\n171\t      - -1.6\n172\t      - -2.5\n173\t      - -2.8\n174\t      - -3.0\n175\t      - 0.34\n176\t    - - Gemma-31B\n177\t      - 3.2\n178\t      - -0.4\n179\t      - -1.0\n180\t      - -2.2\n181\t      - -2.5\n182\t      - -2.8\n183\t      - 0.32\n184\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Benchmark Detection (15% contamination, all families avg)'\n185\t    columns:\n186\t    - benchmark\n187\t    - n_items\n188\t    - avg_d\n189\t    - power_theory\n190\t    - memo_frac\n191\t    rows:\n192\t    - - MMLU\n193\t      - 14042\n194\t      - -2.8\n195\t      - 0.979\n196\t      - 0.35\n197\t    - - HellaSwag\n198\t      - 10042\n199\t      - -1.8\n200\t      - 0.753\n201\t      - 0.33\n202\t    - - GSM8K\n203\t      - 1319\n204\t      - -1.5\n205\t      - 0.591\n206\t      - 0.3\n207\t  figures_description:\n208\t  - 'Heatmap: family × contamination_level → Cohen''s d'\n209\t  - 'Dose-response curves: 4 families, free-θ vs θ-fixed'\n210\t  - Cross-benchmark power comparison with theory overlay\n211\t  analysis: '3 families 足以支撑跨家族泛化 claim。Gemma 若部分失败，以 footnote 说明参数量/ QLoRA 差异。n_items\n212\t    效应与 power theory 一致——这本身强化 Claim 2。Memorization fraction 跨家族一致性 (3pp 差异) 是关键发现，支撑\n213\t    SFT 泛化机制的普适性。\n214\t\n215\t    '\n216\t- name: Leaderboard Audit (ABANDONED)\n217\t  plan_id: exp-leaderboard-audit\n218\t  description: 'Open LLM Leaderboard v1 大规模扫描。已因 MML-EM refit 失败 (a_r=0.111) 而放弃。\n219\t\n220\t    '\n221\t  expected_results:\n222\t    status: ABANDONED\n223\t    reason: a_r=0.111 discrimination failure makes v1-refit IRT parameters unreliable\n224\t    data_availability_noted: true\n225\t    n_models_available: 13000+\n226\t    future_work_mention: true\n227\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下此实验不执行。MML-EM 从 N=63→178 模型重拟合 IRT 参数，discrimination\n228\t    参数 a_r=0.111 远低于 0.2 阈值——经典 IRT 拟合方法在 LLM 数据上失效因为： (1) 样本量仍不足（经典 IRT 需 N>500），(2)\n229\t    LLM response pattern 违反 local independence（同 domain items 相关），(3) 模型能力分布与 IRT\n230\t    假设不匹配。 13K+ 数据可用性写入 Discussion/Future Work 作为 scaling roadmap。\n231\t\n232\t    '\n233\t  tables: []\n234\t  figures_description: []\n235\t  analysis: '放弃是正确决定。论文中将 refit 失败作为 methodological caveat (Claim 3c) 展示——量化经典 IRT\n236\t    与 neural IRT 估计的 sample size gap。\n237\t\n238\t    '\n239\t- name: Natural Experiment (v1 base→chat pairs)\n240\t  plan_id: exp-natural-experiment\n241\t  description: 'v1 leaderboard base→chat model pairs 的 Δlz* 作为 SFT 效应代理。P2-optional。\n242\t\n243\t    '\n244\t  expected_results:\n245\t    n_pairs: 21\n246\t    n_complete_pairs: 9\n247\t    significant_benchmarks: 2\n248\t    hellaswag_mean_deviation: -3.4\n249\t    hellaswag_p: 0.001\n250\t    gsm8k_mean_deviation: 3.9\n251\t    gsm8k_p: 0.009\n252\t    mmlu_p: 0.15\n253\t    arcc_p: 0.38\n254\t    individual_outliers: 0\n255\t    interpretation: systematic SFT effects, not contamination-specific\n256\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 显示系统性 SFT 效应（方向一致的 Δlz* shift） 但无个体\n257\t    pair 出现 benchmark-specific 异常。这是因为 chat 模型的 SFT 训练 普遍改变了 response pattern——HellaSwag\n258\t    (commonsense) 受 instruction tuning 负面影响（降低 person-fit），GSM8K (math) 受益（提高 person-fit）。但用\n259\t    a_r=0.111 的 refit 参数计算的 lz* 本质上退化为 accuracy-like 指标，无法 区分 contamination 与 legitimate\n260\t    SFT improvement。仅 9 个 complete pairs 缺乏统计检验力做细粒度分析。作为 P2 supplementary evidence\n261\t    足够。\n262\t\n263\t    '\n264\t  tables:\n265\t  - name: 'Table: Natural Experiment SFT Effects'\n266\t    columns:\n267\t    - benchmark\n268\t    - mean_delta_lz\n269\t    - t_stat\n270\t    - p_value\n271\t    - interpretation\n272\t    rows:\n273\t    - - HellaSwag\n274\t      - -3.4\n275\t      - -3.97\n276\t      - 0.001\n277\t      - SFT decreases person-fit\n278\t    - - GSM8K\n279\t      - 3.9\n280\t      - 3.35\n281\t      - 0.009\n282\t      - SFT increases person-fit\n283\t    - - MMLU\n284\t      - '+1.2'\n285\t      - 1.54\n286\t      - 0.15\n287\t      - n.s.\n288\t    - - ARC-C\n289\t      - '-0.8'\n290\t      - -0.91\n291\t      - 0.38\n292\t      - n.s.\n293\t  figures_description:\n294\t  - 'Paired dot plot: base vs chat lz* per benchmark (9 complete pairs)'\n295\t  analysis: 'Supplementary evidence only。系统性 SFT 方向差异 (HellaSwag↓, GSM8K↑) 有趣 但因 refit\n296\t    参数质量问题不做强 claim。P2 降级合理。\n297\t\n298\t    '\n299\t- name: v1 IRT Refit Expanded (N≥500)\n300\t  plan_id: exp-v1-irt-refit-expanded\n301\t  description: '扩大 v1 IRT 重拟合样本量至 N≥500，最终关闭 Path D。\n302\t\n303\t    '\n304\t  expected_results:\n305\t    n_models_downloaded: 178\n306\t    a_pearson_r_3pl: 0.127\n307\t    a_pearson_r_2pl: -0.029\n308\t    b_pearson_r_3pl: 0.663\n309\t    conclusion: Path D dead — discrimination failure persists at N=178\n310\t    threshold_met: false\n311\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 N=178 仍无法恢复 discrimination 参数（a_r=0.127, 远低于 0.4 可行阈值）。根本原因不是样本量而是经典\n312\t    MML-EM 拟合方法的结构性限制： (1) LLM response pattern 不满足 local independence——同 domain 1000+\n313\t    items 高度相关，(2) 能力维度 θ 对 LLM 而言不是单一维度——不同 benchmark 需要不同 \"能力\"，(3) N=178 模型虽多于 pilot\n314\t    的 63，但 item 数 14042 远超模型数， 导致 over-determined 系统。b_r=0.663 部分成功因为 difficulty 与\n315\t    accuracy 线性相关——即使模型不多也能恢复。a (discrimination) 需要建模 item 间差异化 响应概率的曲率，这需要更多分布覆盖。Path\n316\t    D 确认关闭。\n317\t\n318\t    '\n319\t  tables:\n320\t  - name: 'Table: IRT Refit Parameter Recovery'\n321\t    columns:\n322\t    - method\n323\t    - n_models\n324\t    - a_r\n325\t    - b_r\n326\t    - conclusion\n327\t    rows:\n328\t    - - 3PL pilot\n329\t      - 63\n330\t      - 0.111\n331\t      - 0.626\n332\t      - dead\n333\t    - - 3PL expanded\n334\t      - 178\n335\t      - 0.127\n336\t      - 0.663\n337\t      - dead\n338\t    - - 2PL expanded\n339\t      - 178\n340\t      - -0.029\n341\t      - 0.572\n342\t      - dead\n343\t  figures_description: []\n344\t  analysis: 'Path D 最终关闭。论文 Claim 3c 中作为 methodological caveat 展示。 关键贡献：量化经典 IRT 与\n345\t    LLM context 的 sample size gap。\n346\t\n347\t    '\n348\t- name: 4PL vs 3PL Ablation\n349\t  plan_id: exp-4pl-ablation\n350\t  description: '4PL vs 3PL(d=1) ablation——量化 feasibility parameter d 对检测的影响。\n351\t\n352\t    '\n353\t  expected_results:\n354\t    far_4pl: 0.05\n355\t    far_3pl: 4.7-16.5%\n356\t    far_2pl: 50-100%\n357\t    mean_power_gain_mmlu: +27pp\n358\t    mean_power_gain_hellaswag: +26pp\n359\t    mean_power_gain_gsm8k: +20pp\n360\t    items_with_d_lt_0.95_mmlu: 46%\n361\t    max_power_gain: +59pp (HellaSwag)\n362\t    deepseek_v3_delta: 357\n363\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 4PL d 参数对检测至关重要。46% MMLU items 有 d<0.95——这些 items\n364\t    的 upper asymptote 低于 1.0，意味着即使能力极高的模型也无法以 100% 概率答对。 忽略 d (设 d=1) 使得 4PL 模型对高能力模型的预测概率系统性偏高，产生虚假\n365\t    aberrance 信号——高能力模型答错一个 d=0.8 的 item 是正常的，但 3PL 认为是 异常。结果：(1) 3PL FAR 膨胀至 4.7-16.5%（benchmark\n366\t    依赖），(2) detection power 平均下降 20-27pp 因为 noise floor 升高，(3) 2PL 更灾难性（FAR 50-100%）\n367\t    因为同时忽略了 guessing parameter c。power gain 在 d<0.8 bucket 最大 (+6.8 to +61.2pp)，d≥0.95\n368\t    时 gain 可忽略。这证明 PSN-IRT 的 4PL 参数化对 LLM contamination detection 而非 academic nicety\n369\t    是必要的。\n370\t\n371\t    '\n372\t  tables:\n373\t  - name: 'Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Power (25% contamination)'\n374\t    columns:\n375\t    - benchmark\n376\t    - power_4pl\n377\t    - power_3pl\n378\t    - gain\n379\t    - pct_items_d_lt_0.95\n380\t    rows:\n381\t    - - MMLU\n382\t      - 0.776\n383\t      - 0.329\n384\t      - +44.7pp\n385\t      - 46%\n386\t    - - HellaSwag\n387\t      - 0.534\n388\t      - 0.28\n389\t      - +25.4pp\n390\t      - 38%\n391\t    - - GSM8K\n392\t      - 0.73\n393\t      - 0.334\n394\t      - +39.6pp\n395\t      - 42%\n396\t    - - ARC-C\n397\t      - 0.132\n398\t      - 0.091\n399\t      - +4.1pp\n400\t      - 28%\n401\t    - - HumanEval\n402\t      - 0.318\n403\t      - 0.165\n404\t      - +15.3pp\n405\t      - 35%\n406\t  figures_description:\n407\t  - 'Side-by-side power curves: 4PL vs 3PL across contamination levels'\n408\t  - 'Scatter: d parameter value vs power gain per item bucket'\n409\t  analysis: '4PL 对 LLM 应用必要性的强证据。回应 R8 reviewer concern。结论：使用 3PL 会丢失约一半检测力。\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t- name: Baseline Comparison (≥5 baselines)\n413\t  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n414\t  description: '在控制实验 ground-truth contaminated models 上比较 IRT-FIT vs ≥5 baselines。\n415\t    包括 ConStat (retest), Min-K%++ (token probs), acc z-score, HT, Guttman/U3。\n416\t\n417\t    '\n418\t  expected_results:\n419\t    model_level_lz_star_d_qwen15: -3.42\n420\t    model_level_ht_d_qwen15: -3.21\n421\t    model_level_guttman_d_qwen15: -0.43\n422\t    model_level_u3_d_qwen15: -0.38\n423\t    model_level_acc_zscore: 160.6\n424\t    ht_vs_lz_star_ratio: 0.94\n425\t    lz_star_vs_guttman_ratio: 8.0\n426\t    constat_retest_auroc: 0.78\n427\t    mink_sft_auroc: 0.6\n428\t    item_level_max_auroc: 0.63\n429\t    item_level_lz_itemwise_auroc: 0.536\n430\t    item_level_irt_residual_auroc: 0.582\n431\t    item_level_lr_cross_auroc: 0.592\n432\t    item_level_rf_oracle_auroc: 0.63\n433\t    n_baselines_beaten: 4\n434\t    n_baselines_total: 6\n435\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心发现：HT 与 lz* 在 model-level detection 上差距很小 (d ratio\n436\t    ~0.94)——HT 仅需 item difficulty，无需完整 4PL 参数化，却达到 comparable 效果。这是因为 model-level\n437\t    aggregation 对 14K items 的 central limit theorem 效应使得 item-level 参数权重差异被平均掉——HT\n438\t    的 uniform weighting 与 lz* 的 a-weighted 方案在大 n 下收敛。lz* vs Guttman/U3 的 8× 差距证明\n439\t    IRT 框架（含 difficulty ordering）优于纯 response pattern 统计。 ConStat retest AUROC=0.78\n440\t    有效但需额外推理轮次（更多信息），符合 detection frontier 叙事。Min-K%++ 在 SFT 上 AUROC=0.60（弱），因为 SFT\n441\t    改变了 token 分布但未产生 memorization-specific 的 perplexity 异常——SFT 后模型对 contaminated\n442\t    items 的 logprob 分布与 generalization 难以区分。Item-level 所有方法 near-random (max 0.63\n443\t    with oracle) 因为 memorization fraction ~35% 意味着仅 1/3 items 产生可检测信号——这种 diffuse\n444\t    signature 只能通过 model-level aggregation 检测。acc z-score 的 z=160 说明它在 controlled\n445\t    setting 下 trivially 有效但无法在 real-world 中区分 contamination 与 legitimate high ability。\n446\t\n447\t    '\n448\t  tables:\n449\t  - name: 'Table: Model-Level Baseline Comparison (Qwen 15% contamination)'\n450\t    columns:\n451\t    - method\n452\t    - info_required\n453\t    - cohens_d\n454\t    - requires_retest\n455\t    - interpretable\n456\t    rows:\n457\t    - - lz* (ours)\n458\t      - binary + 4PL params\n459\t      - -3.42\n460\t      - 'No'\n461\t      - Yes (θ-shift, memo frac)\n462\t    - - HT\n463\t      - binary + item difficulty\n464\t      - -3.21\n465\t      - 'No'\n466\t      - Limited\n467\t    - - Guttman\n468\t      - binary only\n469\t      - -0.43\n470\t      - 'No'\n471\t      - 'No'\n472\t    - - U3\n473\t      - binary only\n474\t      - -0.38\n475\t      - 'No'\n476\t      - 'No'\n477\t    - - acc z-score\n478\t      - binary + population stats\n479\t      - -160.6\n480\t      - 'No'\n481\t      - No (specificity issue)\n482\t    - - ConStat\n483\t      - binary + retest\n484\t      - AUROC=0.78\n485\t      - 'Yes'\n486\t      - Partial\n487\t    - - Min-K%++\n488\t      - token probabilities\n489\t      - AUROC=0.60\n490\t      - 'No'\n491\t      - 'No'\n492\t  - name: 'Table: Item-Level Detection (all methods near-random)'\n493\t    columns:\n494\t    - method\n495\t    - auroc_qwen15\n496\t    - auroc_qwen50\n497\t    - auroc_llama15\n498\t    - auroc_llama50\n499\t    rows:\n500\t    - - lz_itemwise\n501\t      - 0.536\n502\t      - 0.535\n503\t      - 0.528\n504\t      - 0.536\n505\t    - - irt_residual\n506\t      - 0.578\n507\t      - 0.563\n508\t      - 0.582\n509\t      - 0.581\n510\t    - - lr_cross_model\n511\t      - 0.586\n512\t      - 0.567\n513\t      - 0.592\n514\t      - 0.585\n515\t    - - rf_oracle\n516\t      - 0.61\n517\t      - 0.63\n518\t      - 0.615\n519\t      - 0.629\n520\t    - - random\n521\t      - 0.5\n522\t      - 0.5\n523\t      - 0.5\n524\t      - 0.5\n525\t  figures_description:\n526\t  - 'Detection frontier diagram: methods ranked by information access vs detection\n527\t    power'\n528\t  - 'Bar chart: model-level Cohen''s d across all baselines'\n529\t  - 'ROC curves: item-level detection (all near diagonal)'\n530\t  analysis: 'Median 档叙事转向：lz* 的优势不在 raw detection power（HT comparable）而在 interpretability\n531\t    和 framework contribution。n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT\n532\t    comparable 但缺乏 parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting——这些在 MMLU 57\n533\t    subjects 异质性大时理论上更精确。 ConStat 有效但需 retest (更多信息)。\n534\t\n535\t    '\n536\t- name: Multiscale lzm Aggregation\n537\t  plan_id: exp-multiscale-lzm\n538\t  description: '实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合的 标准化\n539\t    lz* 总分。\n540\t\n541\t    '\n542\t  expected_results:\n543\t    lzm_gemini15: 45.2\n544\t    lzm_deepseek_v3: 38.7\n545\t    lzm_qwen_plus: 35.1\n546\t    lzm_doubao: -18.3\n547\t    lzm_mistral: 12.4\n548\t    lzm_correlation_with_max_lz: 0.92\n549\t    lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_clean: 12.8\n550\t    lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_15: 6.5\n551\t    lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_50: 9.2\n552\t    added_value_over_per_benchmark: marginal\n553\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 lzm 提供 per-model 的单一污染严重度指标，但 added value 有限。 lzm\n554\t    本质是各 benchmark lz* 的 variance-weighted sum——由于 MMLU lz* 已经 dominate (n=14042 产生最极端值)，lzm\n555\t    高度相关于 max per-benchmark lz* (r=0.92)。在 PSN-IRT 12-model data 上，lzm 重现已知排序（Gemini-1.5\n556\t    最高）。 在 ctrl-contam 上，因为只有 MMLU 数据，lzm 退化为 lz* itself。理论贡献： 展示 Hong et al. 公式对\n557\t    LLM multi-benchmark 评估的适用性。但 median 档下 不产生 new insight——P2 优先级合理。若 full ctrl-contam\n558\t    覆盖 3 benchmarks， lzm 可显示跨 benchmark aggregation 的 marginal gain。\n559\t\n560\t    '\n561\t  tables:\n562\t  - name: 'Table: lzm vs max-benchmark lz* (PSN-IRT 12 models)'\n563\t    columns:\n564\t    - model\n565\t    - lzm\n566\t    - max_lz_star\n567\t    - dominant_benchmark\n568\t    rows:\n569\t    - - Gemini-1.5\n570\t      - 45.2\n571\t      - 31.8\n572\t      - MMLU\n573\t    - - DeepSeek-V3\n574\t      - 38.7\n575\t      - 25.3\n576\t      - MMLU\n577\t    - - Qwen-Plus\n578\t      - 35.1\n579\t      - 24.5\n580\t      - MMLU\n581\t    - - Doubao-Pro\n582\t      - -18.3\n583\t      - -15.2\n584\t      - HellaSwag\n585\t  figures_description:\n586\t  - 'Scatter: lzm vs max per-benchmark lz* (high correlation)'\n587\t  analysis: 'Appendix material。lzm 在当前数据条件下不改变结论。未来若覆盖更多 benchmarks 且有 cross-benchmark\n588\t    differential contamination，lzm 可显示独立价值。\n589\t\n590\t    '\n591\t- name: Post-RL Hypothesis Test\n592\t  plan_id: exp-post-rl\n593\t  description: 'Qwen3.5-9B 先 SFT 污染再 GRPO 训练，测试 person-fit 是否在 RL 后保持检测力。\n594\t\n595\t    '\n596\t  expected_results:\n597\t    post_rl_lz_star_cohens_d: 1.5\n598\t    post_rl_ht_cohens_d: 1.3\n599\t    post_rl_mia_auroc: 0.52\n600\t    post_rl_mink_auroc: 0.51\n601\t    pre_rl_lz_star_d: -3.42\n602\t    signal_retention_lz: 0.44\n603\t    signal_retention_ht: 0.4\n604\t    rl_steps: 2000\n605\t    reward_type: rule-based (accuracy on held-out)\n606\t    delta_lz_pre_rl: -4.84\n607\t    delta_lz_post_rl: -2.1\n608\t    delta_ht_post_rl: -1.8\n609\t    theta_shift_post_rl: 0.35\n610\t    acc_post_rl: 0.74\n611\t    acc_seen_post_rl: 0.7\n612\t    acc_unseen_post_rl: 0.68\n613\t    memo_frac_post_rl: 0.12\n614\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：post-RL signal partially degrades for ALL person-fit\n615\t    methods。 GRPO 优化使模型学会\"推理\"而非\"记忆\"——RL 的 reward signal 鼓励 generalizable reasoning\n616\t    patterns，这部分平滑了 SFT 注入的 memorization fingerprint。 具体机制：(1) memorization fraction\n617\t    从 ~38% 降至 ~12%——RL 使模型对 seen items 的回答方式从 rote recall 转向 reasoning-based，部分 items\n618\t    不再产生 difficulty-inconsistent response；(2) θ 进一步上升（RL 提升整体能力），吸收 更多 aberrance；(3)\n619\t    但 ~12% items 仍保留 memorization signature——这些是 factual knowledge items 无法通过推理路径解答，只能靠记忆。lz*\n620\t    d=1.5 和 HT d=1.3 均在 [1.0, 2.0] 范围内——detectable 但 effect size 明显弱于 pre-RL。 两者退化幅度相似（signal_retention\n621\t    ~40-44%），说明 RL-induced degradation 作用于 response pattern level（person-fit 家族共享），非统计量特异性。MIA/\n622\t    Min-K++ AUROC ~0.51-0.52（near random）符合 Wang et al. 发现——log-prob 方法在 RL 后完全失效，而\n623\t    person-fit 保留 partial signal。这是 person-fit 作为 family 的 structural advantage，但无法\n624\t    differentiate lz* vs HT。\n625\t\n626\t    '\n627\t  tables:\n628\t  - name: 'Table: Post-RL Detection Power Comparison'\n629\t    columns:\n630\t    - method\n631\t    - pre_rl_d\n632\t    - post_rl_d\n633\t    - retention\n634\t    - info_level\n635\t    rows:\n636\t    - - lz*\n637\t      - -3.42\n638\t      - -1.5\n639\t      - 44%\n640\t      - binary + 4PL\n641\t    - - HT\n642\t      - -3.21\n643\t      - -1.3\n644\t      - 40%\n645\t      - binary + difficulty\n646\t    - - Guttman\n647\t      - -0.43\n648\t      - -0.2\n649\t      - 47%\n650\t      - binary only\n651\t    - - Min-K%++\n652\t      - AUROC=0.60\n653\t      - AUROC=0.51\n654\t      - ~random\n655\t      - token probs\n656\t    - - MIA-loss\n657\t      - AUROC=0.59\n658\t      - AUROC=0.52\n659\t      - ~random\n660\t      - token probs\n661\t  - name: 'Table: Memorization Fraction Degradation'\n662\t    columns:\n663\t    - stage\n664\t    - memo_frac\n665\t    - lz_star\n666\t    - delta_lz\n667\t    - cohens_d\n668\t    rows:\n669\t    - - clean\n670\t      - '-'\n671\t      - 8.68\n672\t      - 0\n673\t      - '-'\n674\t    - - post-SFT (15%)\n675\t      - 0.38\n676\t      - 3.85\n677\t      - -4.84\n678\t      - -3.42\n679\t    - - post-RL\n680\t      - 0.12\n681\t      - 6.58\n682\t      - -2.1\n683\t      - -1.5\n684\t  figures_description:\n685\t  - 'Three-stage waterfall: clean → SFT-contaminated → post-RL lz* trajectory'\n686\t  - 'Bar chart: person-fit family vs log-prob family post-RL retention'\n687\t  - 'Seen/unseen accuracy gap: pre-RL vs post-RL (gap narrows)'\n688\t  analysis: 'Median 档叙事策略：(1) person-fit FAMILY 在 post-RL 保留 detectable signal (d>1.0)，log-prob\n689\t    方法完全失效——class-level advantage 确认；(2) lz* 与 HT 退化幅度相似，无法 empirically differentiate——转用数据无关差异化论证\n690\t    (parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting)；(3) memorization fraction\n691\t    从 38%→12% 量化了 RL 的 \"washing\" 效应——这本身是对 RL alignment 文献的贡献（RL 部分消除 SFT contamination）；(4)\n692\t    论文 claim 从 \"lz* uniquely robust\" 软化为 \"person-fit family robust; lz* uniquely interpretable\"。\n693\t\n694\t    '\n695\t- name: Extra Benchmarks (BBH + MATH)\n696\t  plan_id: exp-extra-benchmarks\n697\t  description: '扩展 benchmark 覆盖：BBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 填充 1K-10K items\n698\t    的 power gap。\n699\t\n700\t    '\n701\t  expected_results:\n702\t    bbh_4pl_available: false\n703\t    math_4pl_available: false\n704\t    bbh_2pl_refit_attempted: true\n705\t    bbh_a_r: 0.15\n706\t    math_a_r: 0.12\n707\t    bbh_power_15pct_sim: 0.68\n708\t    math_power_15pct_sim: 0.62\n709\t    bbh_ctrl_contam_d15: -1.8\n710\t    math_ctrl_contam_d15: -1.2\n711\t    power_gap_filled: partial\n712\t    n_items_range_covered: 1319 (GSM8K) → 6511 (BBH) → 10042 (HellaSwag) → 14042 (MMLU)\n713\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 PSN-IRT 不包含 BBH/MATH 的 4PL 参数——需自行拟合。但自行 拟合面临与 v1-refit\n714\t    相同的问题：discrimination recovery 弱 (a_r ~0.12-0.15)。 Workaround：(1) 仅用 simulation（假设合理\n715\t    4PL 参数分布）预测 power—— BBH 6511 items 在 15% 时 power ~68%（power theory R²=0.957 插值），\n716\t    MATH 5000 items ~62%；(2) 如果有 ctrl-contam 数据，用 PSN-IRT MMLU 参数 的 distributional\n717\t    statistics 生成 synthetic 4PL 参数估计。Ctrl-contam 实际 d 值偏低 (BBH d ~1.8, MATH d ~1.2)\n718\t    因为拟合参数质量不如 PSN-IRT——但仍 在 detectable 范围。填充 power gap 是 partial 的：power theory 插值有效，\n719\t    但缺乏 ground-truth 4PL 参数的直接验证。\n720\t\n721\t    '\n722\t  tables:\n723\t  - name: 'Table: Power Function Validation Across Benchmark Sizes'\n724\t    columns:\n725\t    - benchmark\n726\t    - n_items\n727\t    - power_theory_15pct\n728\t    - power_sim_15pct\n729\t    - power_ctrl_d15\n730\t    rows:\n731\t    - - ARC-C\n732\t      - 295\n733\t      - 0.129\n734\t      - 0.129\n735\t      - 0.5-1.5 (θ-fixed)\n736\t    - - GSM8K\n737\t      - 1319\n738\t      - 0.591\n739\t      - 0.591\n740\t      - '-1.5'\n741\t    - - MATH\n742\t      - 5000\n743\t      - 0.62\n744\t      - ~0.62 (sim)\n745\t      - '-1.2'\n746\t    - - BBH\n747\t      - 6511\n748\t      - 0.68\n749\t      - ~0.68 (sim)\n750\t      - '-1.8'\n751\t    - - HellaSwag\n752\t      - 10042\n753\t      - 0.753\n754\t      - 0.753\n755\t      - '-1.8'\n756\t    - - MMLU\n757\t      - 14042\n758\t      - 0.979\n759\t      - 0.979\n760\t      - '-3.4'\n761\t  figures_description:\n762\t  - Power curve with BBH/MATH points added (theory overlay)\n763\t  analysis: 'Partial contribution。Power theory 插值验证有效但缺乏 PSN-IRT 级别的 4PL ground truth。若\n764\t    PSN-IRT authors 有 BBH/MATH 参数可协作获取——否则仅报告 simulation-based 预测。P2 优先级合理——非论文核心但强化\n765\t    Claim 2。\n766\t\n767\t    '\n768\t- name: Domain-Level Analysis (MMLU subjects)\n769\t  plan_id: exp-domain-analysis\n770\t  description: '按 MMLU subject category 分别计算 person-fit，识别污染的 domain 分布模式。\n771\t\n772\t    '\n773\t  expected_results:\n774\t    gemini_accuracy: 1.0\n775\t    gemini_subjects_flagged: 50/57\n776\t    gemini_domain_concentrated: false\n777\t    gemini_stem_lz: 21.2\n778\t    gemini_humanities_lz: 17.9\n779\t    gemini_social_sciences_lz: 15.9\n780\t    gemini_other_lz: 15.3\n781\t    doubao_negative_lz: true\n782\t    doubao_stem_lz: -2.0\n783\t    doubao_humanities_lz: -13.0\n784\t    doubao_social_sciences_lz: -14.8\n785\t    ctrl_contam_domain_uniform: true\n786\t    ctrl_contam_seen_unseen_per_domain: consistent across domains\n787\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 domain analysis 确认两种 contamination 模式：(1) Gemini-1.5\n788\t    的 uniform 高 lz* 横跨 50/57 subjects——全面 contamination 或极高能力 (acc=100%)，无法区分但 domain\n789\t    均匀性本身是 pattern；(2) Doubao 的 selective negative lz*——Humanities/Social Sciences\n790\t    显示强 negative aberrance (lz* -13 to -15)，暗示这些 domains 的 training data 与 MMLU item\n791\t    distribution 不匹配（答对 hard items 但答错 easy items）。STEM 相对正常 因为 STEM 训练数据覆盖更广。ctrl-contam\n792\t    (QLoRA) 注入的 items 按 random 15% 采样，因此 domain 分布预期 uniform——验证实验设计的内部一致性。 Domain-level\n793\t    分析的附加价值：为 future auditors 提供 \"contamination fingerprinting\" 工具——selective domain\n794\t    contamination 暗示 targeted training。\n795\t\n796\t    '\n797\t  tables:\n798\t  - name: 'Table: Domain-Level lz* Profile (Selected Models)'\n799\t    columns:\n800\t    - model\n801\t    - STEM\n802\t    - Humanities\n803\t    - Social_Sci\n804\t    - Other\n805\t    - pattern\n806\t    rows:\n807\t    - - Gemini-1.5\n808\t      - 21.2\n809\t      - 17.9\n810\t      - 15.9\n811\t      - 15.3\n812\t      - uniform high\n813\t    - - Doubao-Pro\n814\t      - -2.0\n815\t      - -13.0\n816\t      - -14.8\n817\t      - 4.4\n818\t      - selective negative\n819\t    - - Hunyuan-Large\n820\t      - 1.8\n821\t      - 8.5\n822\t      - 13.9\n823\t      - 6.2\n824\t      - social science high\n825\t    - - Yi-Lightning\n826\t      - 48.2\n827\t      - 35.1\n828\t      - 42.5\n829\t      - 38.9\n830\t      - uniform extreme\n831\t  figures_description:\n832\t  - 'Heatmap: model × MMLU domain → lz* (4 categories)'\n833\t  - 'Radar chart: Gemini vs Doubao domain profiles'\n834\t  analysis: 'Appendix or §5.3 subsection。Domain-level 分析支撑 Claim 3b (anomaly profiles)。Selective\n835\t    vs uniform 模式为 contamination typology 提供 mechanistic insight。\n836\t\n837\t    '\n838\t- name: ConStat Comparison (Retest-Based)\n839\t  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n840\t  description: 'ConStat (NeurIPS 2024) retest-based comparison on ctrl-contam models。\n841\t    Part of baseline comparison but requiring additional inference runs。\n842\t\n843\t    '\n844\t  expected_results:\n845\t    constat_retest_auroc: 0.78\n846\t    constat_n_retests: 3\n847\t    constat_gpu_hours: 8\n848\t    constat_vs_lz_star_at_model_level: comparable detection\n849\t    constat_information_cost: 3× inference budget\n850\t    constat_specificity: higher than acc z-score\n851\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 ConStat 在 model-level 检测上 AUROC=0.78——有效但不如 lz* 的\n852\t    d=3.4 直接。ConStat 的 retest 设计需要 rephrased items 和多次推理， 本质上是用\"更多信息\"换取\"更确定的判断\"。AUROC\n853\t    0.78 而非更高是因为： (1) QLoRA SFT 的 memorization 是 partial (~35%)——rephrased items 的\n854\t    response 变化不如 verbatim 记忆那么 dramatic；(2) SFT 泛化效应使得部分 seen items 即使 rephrased\n855\t    也答对——这降低了 retest 的 sensitivity。 关键对比：lz* 用 zero 额外推理达到 comparable 检测力——这是 minimal-information\n856\t    operating point 的核心价值。ConStat 在 detection frontier 上位于 \"binary + retest\" 层级，高于\n857\t    lz* 的 \"binary only\" 但低于 \"token probs\" 层级。\n858\t\n859\t    '\n860\t  tables: []\n861\t  figures_description: []\n862\t  analysis: 'Integrated into baseline comparison table。ConStat 结果强化 detection frontier\n863\t    叙事——更多信息确实有帮助但 marginal gain 不大。\n864\t\n865\t    '\n866\t- name: MIA/Min-K++ on SFT Contamination\n867\t  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n868\t  description: 'Min-K%++ 和 MIA-loss 在 SFT-contaminated 模型上的表现。\n869\t\n870\t    '\n871\t  expected_results:\n872\t    mink_sft_auroc: 0.61\n873\t    mia_loss_sft_auroc: 0.59\n874\t    mink_base_auroc: 0.49\n875\t    mia_loss_base_auroc: 0.49\n876\t    mink_post_rl_auroc: 0.51\n877\t    interpretation: SFT produces weak token-level signal, RL washes it\n878\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 Min-K%++ 在 SFT contamination 上 AUROC=0.61——高于 random\n879\t    但远低于 lz* 的 model-level detection (d=3.4)。SFT 确实在 token-level 留下微弱信号（seen items\n880\t    的 perplexity 略低），但 QLoRA 的 low-rank constraint 限制了 memorization 精度——模型学到的是 \"pattern-level\"\n881\t    而非 \"token-level\" 的记忆，导致 Min-K%++ 这种依赖 token-level anomaly 的 方法效果有限。这与 MIA-loss\n882\t    类似 (AUROC=0.59)——两者本质上测量同一信号 (token probability anomaly) 的不同 summary。Base model\n883\t    (未 SFT) 上两者 ~random (0.49) 因为没有 memorization 信号。Post-RL 时 AUROC 回到 ~0.51 (near\n884\t    random)——RL 的 distributional shift 完全掩盖了残余的 token-level signal，与 Wang et al. (2025)\n885\t    一致。\n886\t\n887\t    '\n888\t  tables:\n889\t  - name: 'Table: Token-Level Methods Across Training Stages'\n890\t    columns:\n891\t    - method\n892\t    - base_auroc\n893\t    - sft_auroc\n894\t    - post_rl_auroc\n895\t    rows:\n896\t    - - Min-K%++\n897\t      - 0.49\n898\t      - 0.61\n899\t      - 0.51\n900\t    - - MIA-loss\n901\t      - 0.49\n902\t      - 0.59\n903\t      - 0.52\n904\t    - - PPL-based\n905\t      - 0.5\n906\t      - 0.56\n907\t      - 0.5\n908\t  figures_description:\n909\t  - 'ROC curves: Min-K++/MIA across training stages'\n910\t  analysis: 'Confirms binary-only person-fit is NOT inferior to token-prob methods\n911\t    for SFT contamination。Token methods'' weakness validates the minimal-information\n912\t    framing——more information (token probs) doesn''t necessarily help when the contamination\n913\t    mechanism is SFT-style.\n914\t\n915\t    '\n916\t- name: ARC-C Benchmark Validation (Small Benchmark)\n917\t  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n918\t  description: 'ARC-Challenge (295 items) 上的控制实验——验证 small benchmark 检测极限。\n919\t\n920\t    '\n921\t  expected_results:\n922\t    arcc_clean_lz: -5.5\n923\t    arcc_contam15_lz: -4.9\n924\t    arcc_contam50_lz: -4.6\n925\t    arcc_delta_lz_15: 0.6\n926\t    arcc_delta_lz_50: 0.9\n927\t    arcc_cohens_d_15_free: -0.5\n928\t    arcc_cohens_d_50_free: -0.8\n929\t    arcc_theta_fixed_d_15: 0.8\n930\t    arcc_theta_fixed_d_50: 1.2\n931\t    arcc_power_theory_15: 0.129\n932\t    arcc_memo_frac: 0.3\n933\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 ARC-C (295 items) 在 free-θ 下检测力很弱 (d ~0.5 at 15%)\n934\t    因为 power theory 预测仅 12.9% power。295 items 的 lz* 方差大——noise floor 高导致 signal/noise\n935\t    ratio 低。θ-fixed 改善至 d ~0.8-1.2 因为消除了 θ-shift confound，但仍远低于 MMLU 的 d=3.4。Memorization\n936\t    fraction ~30% 意味着 15% contamination 仅 ~44 items 被记忆——在 295 items 中产生的 pattern\n937\t    distortion 不够大。这与 power theory 的 min_items_15pct_80power =7958 一致——ARC-C 远低于此阈值。θ-fixed\n938\t    analysis 的 arcc_theta_fixed_d 在 [0.5, 1.5] 范围内——detectable 但效应弱。这是一个\"honest characterization\"\n939\t    而非限制——小 benchmark 的检测力弱是信息论预期。\n940\t\n941\t    '\n942\t  tables:\n943\t  - name: 'Table: ARC-C Detection (Small Benchmark Regime)'\n944\t    columns:\n945\t    - condition\n946\t    - lz_star\n947\t    - delta_lz\n948\t    - d_free\n949\t    - d_theta_fixed\n950\t    rows:\n951\t    - - clean (mean)\n952\t      - -5.5\n953\t      - 0\n954\t      - '-'\n955\t      - '-'\n956\t    - - contam_15\n957\t      - -4.9\n958\t      - 0.6\n959\t      - -0.5\n960\t      - 0.8\n961\t    - - contam_50\n962\t      - -4.6\n963\t      - 0.9\n964\t      - -0.8\n965\t      - 1.2\n966\t  figures_description:\n967\t  - Power curve with ARC-C highlighted as 'small benchmark regime'\n968\t  analysis: 'ARC-C 结果验证 power theory 预测——小 benchmark 检测力弱是理论预期。 θ-fixed 部分补偿但不改变根本限制。论文中作为\n969\t    Claim 2 的支撑证据—— detection power 与 n_items 的关系在实际数据中得到验证。\n970\t\n971\t    '\n972\t- name: HT vs lz* Post-RL Differentiation\n973\t  plan_id: exp-post-rl\n974\t  description: 'Post-RL 条件下 HT 与 lz* 的 differential robustness 测试。\n975\t\n976\t    '\n977\t  expected_results:\n978\t    lz_star_post_rl_d: 1.5\n979\t    ht_post_rl_d: 1.3\n980\t    lz_star_ht_ratio_post_rl: 1.15\n981\t    lz_star_ht_ratio_pre_rl: 1.07\n982\t    differentiation_significant: false\n983\t    differentiation_p_value: 0.35\n984\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心预期：lz* 和 HT post-RL 退化幅度相似，差异不显著 (p=0.35)。 ratio 从\n985\t    pre-RL 1.07 微升至 1.15——lz* 略好但 n=1 (单一模型) 条件下无法 得出统计结论。原因：post-RL 的 signal degradation\n986\t    作用于 response pattern level——RL 改变了模型对 items 的作答方式（从记忆转向推理），这一变化对所有 基于 response\n987\t    pattern 的统计量影响相似。lz* 的 4PL weighting 在 large n (14K items) 下的优势被 RL-induced noise\n988\t    部分抵消。HT 的 robustness 来自其 simplicity——仅依赖 difficulty ordering，RL 对 difficulty ordering\n989\t    的扰动 较小。结论：无法通过 post-RL 实验 empirically differentiate lz* vs HT—— 转用数据无关差异化策略。\n990\t\n991\t    '\n992\t  tables:\n993\t  - name: 'Table: lz* vs HT Post-RL Comparison'\n994\t    columns:\n995\t    - statistic\n996\t    - pre_rl_d\n997\t    - post_rl_d\n998\t    - retention\n999\t    - ratio_lz_over_ht\n1000\t    rows:\n1001\t    - - lz*\n1002\t      - -3.42\n1003\t      - -1.5\n1004\t      - 44%\n1005\t      - '-'\n1006\t    - - HT\n1007\t      - -3.21\n1008\t      - -1.3\n1009\t      - 40%\n1010\t      - '-'\n1011\t    - - ratio\n1012\t      - 1.07\n1013\t      - 1.15\n1014\t      - '-'\n1015\t      - n.s. (p=0.35)\n1016\t  figures_description:\n1017\t  - 'Paired bar chart: lz* vs HT pre/post-RL with error bars'\n1018\t  analysis: 'Median 档叙事应对（对应 R12 reviewer concern）：empirical differentiation 失败 →\n1019\t    激活数据无关差异化三论证：(i) parametric null N(0,1)——bootstrap 已验证 lz* null 分布 mean=0.09/std=1.00，HT\n1020\t    无此性质，需 per-case bootstrap； (ii) Snijders correction Var*=Var_l - C²/I(θ) 补偿 θ\n1021\t    估计误差——尤其在 θ-fixed 不可用时 (e.g., retrospective audit without clean baseline)； (iii)\n1022\t    4PL a-weighting 在 MMLU 57 subjects 高异质性下理论更精确——虽然 empirical d 差异不显著，但信息论上 lz*\n1023\t    使用了更多 item-level information。 论文应坦诚报告并将这些论证置于 Discussion §6。\n1024\t\n1025\t    '\n1026\t- name: Mistral n=1 Supporting Evidence\n1027\t  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n1028\t  description: 'Mistral-7B-v0.3 单 clean seed 控制实验——作为第三个 family 的 supporting evidence。\n1029\t\n1030\t    '\n1031\t  expected_results:\n1032\t    mistral_clean_lz: 5.42\n1033\t    mistral_contam15_lz: -1.38\n1034\t    mistral_contam50_lz: -3.15\n1035\t    mistral_delta_lz_15: -6.8\n1036\t    mistral_delta_lz_50: -8.57\n1037\t    mistral_acc_clean: 0.514\n1038\t    mistral_contam15_acc: 0.595\n1039\t    mistral_memo_frac_15: 0.34\n1040\t    mistral_n_clean_seeds: 1\n1041\t    mistral_cohens_d_estimate: N/A (n=1, no variance estimate)\n1042\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档 Mistral 仅 n=1 clean seed——无法计算 Cohen''s d 或 CI。但 Δlz*=-6.80\n1043\t    (15%) 的绝对值比 Qwen (-4.84) 和 Llama (-2.85) 更大，因为 Mistral 是最弱模型 (acc=0.514)——低能力模型受\n1044\t    contamination 的 response pattern distortion 更大（baseline 答错很多 items，contamination\n1045\t    后这些 items 突然答对，产生更极端的 aberrance）。Mistral baseline lz*=5.42 (正值) 意味着 clean model\n1046\t    已经 slightly over-consistent——contamination 后 lz* 翻转至负值 (-1.38) 说明 aberrance signal\n1047\t    足够强。作为 n=1 supporting evidence 而非 primary validation——论文中明确标注 \"single-seed, indicative\"。跨三个\n1048\t    family (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 的 detection success 足以支撑 n_families_validated=3。\n1049\t\n1050\t    '\n1051\t  tables:\n1052\t  - name: 'Table: Mistral Supporting Evidence (n=1)'\n1053\t    columns:\n1054\t    - condition\n1055\t    - lz_star\n1056\t    - delta_lz\n1057\t    - acc\n1058\t    - theta\n1059\t    - memo_frac\n1060\t    rows:\n1061\t    - - clean\n1062\t      - 5.42\n1063\t      - 0\n1064\t      - 0.514\n1065\t      - -1.157\n1066\t      - '-'\n1067\t    - - contam_15\n1068\t      - -1.38\n1069\t      - -6.8\n1070\t      - 0.595\n1071\t      - -0.713\n1072\t      - 0.34\n1073\t    - - contam_50\n1074\t      - -3.15\n1075\t      - -8.57\n1076\t      - 0.673\n1077\t      - -0.303\n1078\t      - 0.29\n1079\t  figures_description:\n1080\t  - 'Cross-family Δlz* comparison: Qwen vs Llama vs Mistral (indicating n=1 for Mistral)'\n1081\t  analysis: 'Supporting evidence。n=1 不支持独立 claim 但与 Qwen/Llama 一致的方向性 结果增强跨家族泛化叙事。注意\n1082\t    Mistral 的 Δlz* 绝对值更大反映的是低能力 模型的更强 contamination signal——与 power theory 一致（低 θ\n1083\t    baseline → 更大 response pattern shift）。\n1084\t\n1085\t    '\n1086\t- name: Full Baseline Comparison Table (Frontier Ranking)\n1087\t  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n1088\t  description: 'Detection frontier 完整排名表——所有方法按信息访问层级排列。\n1089\t\n1090\t    '\n1091\t  expected_results:\n1092\t    n_baselines_total: 7\n1093\t    n_baselines_beaten_at_model_level: 4\n1094\t    frontier_ranking:\n1095\t      binary_only:\n1096\t      - Guttman (d=0.43)\n1097\t      - U3 (d=0.38)\n1098\t      - random (d=0)\n1099\t      binary_plus_difficulty:\n1100\t      - HT (d=3.21)\n1101\t      binary_plus_4pl:\n1102\t      - lz* (d=3.42)\n1103\t      binary_plus_retest:\n1104\t      - ConStat (AUROC=0.78)\n1105\t      token_probs:\n1106\t      - Min-K%++ (AUROC=0.61)\n1107\t      - MIA-loss (AUROC=0.59)\n1108\t    key_comparison: person-fit family (HT + lz*) >> pure binary (Guttman/U3) >> token-prob\n1109\t      (Min-K++)\n1110\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档 frontier ranking 清晰呈现信息层级与检测力的关系：(1) 纯 binary (Guttman/U3)\n1111\t    最弱因为不利用 item difficulty 信息——仅看 response pattern 的 non-randomness，无法区分 high-ability\n1112\t    与 contamination；(2) binary + difficulty (HT) 跳跃式提升至 d=3.21——difficulty ordering\n1113\t    是关键信息， 让统计量能识别 \"答对不该答对的题\"；(3) binary + 4PL (lz*) 在 HT 基础上 marginal gain——a/c/d\n1114\t    参数的额外信息在 14K items 下被 averaging 稀释； (4) token-prob methods 反而弱于 binary person-fit——说明\n1115\t    \"更多信息\" 不等于 \"更好检测\"，信息类型比信息量重要。SFT contamination 的 token-level signal 很弱 (memorization\n1116\t    fraction ~35%)，而 response-pattern-level signal 通过 14K items 聚合后很强。这是论文的核心 insight\n1117\t    之一。\n1118\t\n1119\t    '\n1120\t  tables:\n1121\t  - name: 'Table: Detection Frontier Ranking'\n1122\t    columns:\n1123\t    - method\n1124\t    - info_access\n1125\t    - model_d_or_auroc\n1126\t    - item_auroc\n1127\t    - extra_cost\n1128\t    - interpretable\n1129\t    rows:\n1130\t    - - lz* (ours)\n1131\t      - binary + 4PL params\n1132\t      - d=-3.42\n1133\t      - 0.536\n1134\t      - 0 (calibrated params available)\n1135\t      - 'Yes'\n1136\t    - - HT\n1137\t      - binary + difficulty\n1138\t      - d=-3.21\n1139\t      - N/A\n1140\t      - 0\n1141\t      - Limited\n1142\t    - - acc z-score\n1143\t      - binary + pop stats\n1144\t      - z=160.6\n1145\t      - N/A\n1146\t      - 0\n1147\t      - No (no specificity)\n1148\t    - - ConStat\n1149\t      - binary + retest\n1150\t      - AUROC=0.78\n1151\t      - N/A\n1152\t      - 3× inference\n1153\t      - Partial\n1154\t    - - Min-K%++\n1155\t      - token probs\n1156\t      - AUROC=0.61\n1157\t      - N/A\n1158\t      - API access\n1159\t      - 'No'\n1160\t    - - MIA-loss\n1161\t      - token probs\n1162\t      - AUROC=0.59\n1163\t      - N/A\n1164\t      - API access\n1165\t      - 'No'\n1166\t    - - Guttman/U3\n1167\t      - binary only\n1168\t      - d=-0.43\n1169\t      - N/A\n1170\t      - 0\n1171\t      - 'No'\n1172\t    - - random\n1173\t      - none\n1174\t      - d=0\n1175\t      - 0.5\n1176\t      - 0\n1177\t      - 'No'\n1178\t  figures_description:\n1179\t  - 'Detection frontier diagram: x=information access level, y=detection power, bubble\n1180\t    size=interpretability'\n1181\t  analysis: 'n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT tied。ConStat effective\n1182\t    but higher info cost。Acc z-score 不 comparable (no specificity)。 Total ≥5 baselines\n1183\t    满足同行中位数要求。\n1184\t\n1185\t    '\n1186\t- name: Gemma-4-31B Controlled Contamination (Conditional)\n1187\t  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n1188\t  description: 'Gemma-4-31B 控制实验——第四个 family，median 档下可能部分失败。\n1189\t\n1190\t    '\n1191\t  expected_results:\n1192\t    gemma_training_stable: uncertain\n1193\t    gemma_qlora_rank: 64\n1194\t    gemma_gpu_hours: 20\n1195\t    gemma_clean_lz: 3.2\n1196\t    gemma_contam15_d: -2.2\n1197\t    gemma_contam50_d: -2.8\n1198\t    gemma_partial_failure_risk: 0.35\n1199\t    gemma_memo_frac: 0.32\n1200\t    fallback: drop to 3 families if training unstable\n1201\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档 Gemma-4-31B 是最不确定的实验。31B 参数量显著大于其他三个 (7-9B)， QLoRA 行为可能不同：(1)\n1202\t    rank=64 的 low-rank adaptation 在 31B 模型上 adaptation 比例更小——可能需要更多 epochs 或更高 rank；(2)\n1203\t    Gemma 架构 (Google) 与 Qwen/Llama/Mistral 不同——可能有不同的 SFT 泛化特性； (3) 训练不稳定风险 ~35%（loss\n1204\t    divergence or poor convergence）。如果成功， d ~2.2-2.8 处于可接受范围。如果部分失败（如某些 contamination\n1205\t    levels 不收敛）， 降级为 footnote evidence。3 families (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 已足够支撑 cross-family\n1206\t    claim——Gemma 是 bonus。Memorization fraction 可能略低 (0.32) 因为大模型 QLoRA 的 effective\n1207\t    capacity 更分散。\n1208\t\n1209\t    '\n1210\t  tables:\n1211\t  - name: 'Table: Gemma Conditional Results'\n1212\t    columns:\n1213\t    - condition\n1214\t    - lz_star\n1215\t    - delta_lz\n1216\t    - d_estimate\n1217\t    - training_status\n1218\t    rows:\n1219\t    - - clean\n1220\t      - 3.2\n1221\t      - 0\n1222\t      - '-'\n1223\t      - stable\n1224\t    - - contam_15\n1225\t      - ~0.5\n1226\t      - '-2.7'\n1227\t      - -2.2\n1228\t      - stable/unstable\n1229\t    - - contam_50\n1230\t      - ~-0.8\n1231\t      - '-4.0'\n1232\t      - -2.8\n1233\t      - stable/unstable\n1234\t  figures_description: []\n1235\t  analysis: Conditional on training stability。如果成功 → n_families_validated=4 (bonus)。如果失败\n1236\t    → 3 families 已足够，Gemma 的 scale difference (31B vs 7-9B) 写入 Limitations 作为 future\n1237\t    work。\n1238\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64764f77-fdee-43b3-8ca5-4f585dd5c649","uuid":"0a9fcbd3-1dfe-49ea-850f-f55d5684e515","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:11:46.222Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122444/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'IRT person-fit provides a principled contamination detection\n  framework at the minimal-information operating point, with unique mechanistic interpretability\n  (θ-shift analysis, memorization fraction quantification, parametric null distribution).\n  While simpler statistics (HT) achieve comparable raw detection power, lz* offers:\n  (i) calibrated hypothesis testing via known null N(0,1), (ii) Snijders correction\n  for θ estimation error, (iii) full 4PL item-heterogeneity weighting critical for\n  multi-domain benchmarks like MMLU. Post-RL robustness is demonstrated but shared\n  across the person-fit family — the structural immunity to distributional shifts\n  is a class-level advantage over log-prob methods. Claims soften from ''lz* uniquely\n  robust'' to ''person-fit family robust; lz* uniquely interpretable.''\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen)\n  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam-pilot\n  description: 'Qwen3.5-9B × 4 conditions (0%-seed1/0%-seed2/15%/50%) × MMLU only.\n    Go/no-go 信号实验。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    clean_seed1_lz_star: 8.5\n    clean_seed2_lz_star: 7.9\n    clean_mean: 8.2\n    clean_std: 0.42\n    contam_15_lz_star: 4.1\n    contam_50_lz_star: 7.0\n    delta_lz_star_15: -4.1\n    delta_lz_star_50: -1.2\n    cohens_d_contam15: -3.2\n    cohens_d_contam50: -1.1\n    contam_15_acc: 0.72\n    contam_50_acc: 0.76\n    memorization_fraction_15: 0.36\n    memorization_fraction_50: 0.28\n    seen_lz_star_15: 0.3\n    unseen_lz_star_15: 3.2\n    theta_shift_15: 0.25\n    theta_shift_50: 0.45\n    theta_fixed_contam15_lz: 11.5\n    theta_fixed_contam50_lz: 17.8\n    theta_fixed_ratio: 2.9\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 Qwen 控制实验预期产生强效应但 free-θ 下 50% contamination 出现 non-monotonicity。Qwen\n    baseline lz* 高 (~8-9) 因其 response pattern 与 4PL 预测高度一致但非完美匹配；15% 污染产生明显 aberrance（memorization\n    fraction ~36% 意味着约 1/3 seen items 被记忆，产生 difficulty-inconsistent correct responses）。\n    50% 条件下 θ-shift 吸收大量 aberrance 信号导致 free-θ d 值下降至 ~1.1，但 θ-fixed 恢复单调性（ratio ~2.9）。这与\n    Qwen 高 baseline misfit (lz*~8.5) 交互——高 baseline 模型更容易出现 non-monotonicity 因为 θ\n    估计对 response pattern 变化更敏感。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Qwen Pilot Controlled Contamination Results'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - lz_star\n    - delta_lz_star\n    - cohens_d\n    - acc\n    - theta_mle\n    - lz_star_fixed\n    - memo_frac\n    rows:\n    - - clean_s1\n      - 8.5\n      - 0\n      - '-'\n      - 0.678\n      - -0.1\n      - '-'\n      - '-'\n    - - clean_s2\n      - 7.9\n      - 0\n      - '-'\n      - 0.676\n      - -0.11\n      - '-'\n      - '-'\n    - - contam_15\n      - 4.1\n      - -4.1\n      - -3.2\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.15\n      - 11.5\n      - 0.36\n    - - contam_50\n      - 7.0\n      - -1.2\n      - -1.1\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.35\n      - 17.8\n      - 0.28\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: clean vs contam_15 vs contam_50 lz* (free-θ vs θ-fixed)'\n  - 'Scatter: seen vs unseen item lz* contribution at 15% contamination'\n  analysis: 'Go 信号确认。|d|>2 at 15% 足以支撑 Claim 1。Non-monotonicity 在 free-θ 下出现 是预期的，θ-fixed\n    恢复单调性是方法论贡献。Memorization fraction ~36% 与 SFT generalization 一致——QLoRA 仅记忆约 1/3\n    注入 items，其余通过泛化提升。\n\n    '\n- name: Full Controlled Contamination (4 Families)\n  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n  description: 'Qwen3.5-9B + Gemma-4-31B + Llama-3.1-8B + Mistral-7B-v0.3 × 6 levels\n    (0/5/10/15/25/50%) × MMLU + GSM8K + HellaSwag。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_families_validated: 3\n    qwen_mmlu_d15: -3.4\n    qwen_mmlu_d50: -1.0\n    llama_mmlu_d15: -2.9\n    llama_mmlu_d50: -3.3\n    mistral_mmlu_d15: -2.5\n    mistral_mmlu_d50: -3.0\n    gemma_mmlu_d15: -2.2\n    gemma_mmlu_d50: -2.8\n    gemma_note: Gemma 31B 参数量大，QLoRA 效率不同，可能需调参或 drop\n    gsm8k_avg_d15: -1.5\n    gsm8k_avg_d50: -2.0\n    hellaswag_avg_d15: -1.8\n    hellaswag_avg_d50: -2.5\n    cross_family_memo_frac_range:\n    - 0.3\n    - 0.4\n    cross_family_memo_frac_mean: 0.35\n    dose_response_monotonic_theta_fixed: true\n    dose_response_monotonic_free: model-dependent\n    n_conditions_total: 72\n    n_conditions_significant: 55\n    small_benchmark_weakness: GSM8K (1319 items) d ~1.5 at 15%, below MMLU\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 3/4 families 成功验证（n_families_validated=3）。Gemma-4-31B\n    因 参数量大且 QLoRA rank 可能不足，存在训练不稳定或效果弱化风险——median 档下 Gemma 可能仅提供 partial 结果或需 downgrade\n    为 supporting evidence。跨 benchmark 差异反映 n_items 效应（MMLU 14042 >> GSM8K 1319）——power\n    theory 预测 GSM8K 在 15% 仅有 ~59% power，对应 d ~1.5。HellaSwag (10042 items) 介于两者 之间。Memorization\n    fraction 跨家族一致 (~35%) 是 SFT 机制的稳定性质， 不依赖模型架构——QLoRA 的泛化模式相似因为都是 low-rank adaptation。Free-θ\n    non-monotonicity 仅出现在高 baseline lz* 模型（Qwen, Mistral），Llama (baseline ~0) 保持单调。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Family Detection Summary (MMLU, θ-free)'\n    columns:\n    - family\n    - clean_lz\n    - d_5pct\n    - d_10pct\n    - d_15pct\n    - d_25pct\n    - d_50pct\n    - memo_frac_15\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen-7B\n      - 8.7\n      - -0.8\n      - -1.8\n      - -3.4\n      - -2.8\n      - -1.0\n      - 0.38\n    - - Llama-8B\n      - -0.1\n      - -0.5\n      - -1.5\n      - -2.9\n      - -3.1\n      - -3.3\n      - 0.35\n    - - Mistral-7B\n      - 5.4\n      - -0.7\n      - -1.6\n      - -2.5\n      - -2.8\n      - -3.0\n      - 0.34\n    - - Gemma-31B\n      - 3.2\n      - -0.4\n      - -1.0\n      - -2.2\n      - -2.5\n      - -2.8\n      - 0.32\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Benchmark Detection (15% contamination, all families avg)'\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - n_items\n    - avg_d\n    - power_theory\n    - memo_frac\n    rows:\n    - - MMLU\n      - 14042\n      - -2.8\n      - 0.979\n      - 0.35\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 10042\n      - -1.8\n      - 0.753\n      - 0.33\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 1319\n      - -1.5\n      - 0.591\n      - 0.3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: family × contamination_level → Cohen''s d'\n  - 'Dose-response curves: 4 families, free-θ vs θ-fixed'\n  - Cross-benchmark power comparison with theory overlay\n  analysis: '3 families 足以支撑跨家族泛化 claim。Gemma 若部分失败，以 footnote 说明参数量/ QLoRA 差异。n_items\n    效应与 power theory 一致——这本身强化 Claim 2。Memorization fraction 跨家族一致性 (3pp 差异) 是关键发现，支撑\n    SFT 泛化机制的普适性。\n\n    '\n- name: Leaderboard Audit (ABANDONED)\n  plan_id: exp-leaderboard-audit\n  description: 'Open LLM Leaderboard v1 大规模扫描。已因 MML-EM refit 失败 (a_r=0.111) 而放弃。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: ABANDONED\n    reason: a_r=0.111 discrimination failure makes v1-refit IRT parameters unreliable\n    data_availability_noted: true\n    n_models_available: 13000+\n    future_work_mention: true\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下此实验不执行。MML-EM 从 N=63→178 模型重拟合 IRT 参数，discrimination\n    参数 a_r=0.111 远低于 0.2 阈值——经典 IRT 拟合方法在 LLM 数据上失效因为： (1) 样本量仍不足（经典 IRT 需 N>500），(2)\n    LLM response pattern 违反 local independence（同 domain items 相关），(3) 模型能力分布与 IRT\n    假设不匹配。 13K+ 数据可用性写入 Discussion/Future Work 作为 scaling roadmap。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '放弃是正确决定。论文中将 refit 失败作为 methodological caveat (Claim 3c) 展示——量化经典 IRT\n    与 neural IRT 估计的 sample size gap。\n\n    '\n- name: Natural Experiment (v1 base→chat pairs)\n  plan_id: exp-natural-experiment\n  description: 'v1 leaderboard base→chat model pairs 的 Δlz* 作为 SFT 效应代理。P2-optional。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_pairs: 21\n    n_complete_pairs: 9\n    significant_benchmarks: 2\n    hellaswag_mean_deviation: -3.4\n    hellaswag_p: 0.001\n    gsm8k_mean_deviation: 3.9\n    gsm8k_p: 0.009\n    mmlu_p: 0.15\n    arcc_p: 0.38\n    individual_outliers: 0\n    interpretation: systematic SFT effects, not contamination-specific\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 显示系统性 SFT 效应（方向一致的 Δlz* shift） 但无个体\n    pair 出现 benchmark-specific 异常。这是因为 chat 模型的 SFT 训练 普遍改变了 response pattern——HellaSwag\n    (commonsense) 受 instruction tuning 负面影响（降低 person-fit），GSM8K (math) 受益（提高 person-fit）。但用\n    a_r=0.111 的 refit 参数计算的 lz* 本质上退化为 accuracy-like 指标，无法 区分 contamination 与 legitimate\n    SFT improvement。仅 9 个 complete pairs 缺乏统计检验力做细粒度分析。作为 P2 supplementary evidence\n    足够。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Natural Experiment SFT Effects'\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - mean_delta_lz\n    - t_stat\n    - p_value\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - -3.4\n      - -3.97\n      - 0.001\n      - SFT decreases person-fit\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 3.9\n      - 3.35\n      - 0.009\n      - SFT increases person-fit\n    - - MMLU\n      - '+1.2'\n      - 1.54\n      - 0.15\n      - n.s.\n    - - ARC-C\n      - '-0.8'\n      - -0.91\n      - 0.38\n      - n.s.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired dot plot: base vs chat lz* per benchmark (9 complete pairs)'\n  analysis: 'Supplementary evidence only。系统性 SFT 方向差异 (HellaSwag↓, GSM8K↑) 有趣 但因 refit\n    参数质量问题不做强 claim。P2 降级合理。\n\n    '\n- name: v1 IRT Refit Expanded (N≥500)\n  plan_id: exp-v1-irt-refit-expanded\n  description: '扩大 v1 IRT 重拟合样本量至 N≥500，最终关闭 Path D。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_downloaded: 178\n    a_pearson_r_3pl: 0.127\n    a_pearson_r_2pl: -0.029\n    b_pearson_r_3pl: 0.663\n    conclusion: Path D dead — discrimination failure persists at N=178\n    threshold_met: false\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 N=178 仍无法恢复 discrimination 参数（a_r=0.127, 远低于 0.4 可行阈值）。根本原因不是样本量而是经典\n    MML-EM 拟合方法的结构性限制： (1) LLM response pattern 不满足 local independence——同 domain 1000+\n    items 高度相关，(2) 能力维度 θ 对 LLM 而言不是单一维度——不同 benchmark 需要不同 \"能力\"，(3) N=178 模型虽多于 pilot\n    的 63，但 item 数 14042 远超模型数， 导致 over-determined 系统。b_r=0.663 部分成功因为 difficulty 与\n    accuracy 线性相关——即使模型不多也能恢复。a (discrimination) 需要建模 item 间差异化 响应概率的曲率，这需要更多分布覆盖。Path\n    D 确认关闭。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: IRT Refit Parameter Recovery'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - n_models\n    - a_r\n    - b_r\n    - conclusion\n    rows:\n    - - 3PL pilot\n      - 63\n      - 0.111\n      - 0.626\n      - dead\n    - - 3PL expanded\n      - 178\n      - 0.127\n      - 0.663\n      - dead\n    - - 2PL expanded\n      - 178\n      - -0.029\n      - 0.572\n      - dead\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Path D 最终关闭。论文 Claim 3c 中作为 methodological caveat 展示。 关键贡献：量化经典 IRT 与\n    LLM context 的 sample size gap。\n\n    '\n- name: 4PL vs 3PL Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-4pl-ablation\n  description: '4PL vs 3PL(d=1) ablation——量化 feasibility parameter d 对检测的影响。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    far_4pl: 0.05\n    far_3pl: 4.7-16.5%\n    far_2pl: 50-100%\n    mean_power_gain_mmlu: +27pp\n    mean_power_gain_hellaswag: +26pp\n    mean_power_gain_gsm8k: +20pp\n    items_with_d_lt_0.95_mmlu: 46%\n    max_power_gain: +59pp (HellaSwag)\n    deepseek_v3_delta: 357\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 4PL d 参数对检测至关重要。46% MMLU items 有 d<0.95——这些 items\n    的 upper asymptote 低于 1.0，意味着即使能力极高的模型也无法以 100% 概率答对。 忽略 d (设 d=1) 使得 4PL 模型对高能力模型的预测概率系统性偏高，产生虚假\n    aberrance 信号——高能力模型答错一个 d=0.8 的 item 是正常的，但 3PL 认为是 异常。结果：(1) 3PL FAR 膨胀至 4.7-16.5%（benchmark\n    依赖），(2) detection power 平均下降 20-27pp 因为 noise floor 升高，(3) 2PL 更灾难性（FAR 50-100%）\n    因为同时忽略了 guessing parameter c。power gain 在 d<0.8 bucket 最大 (+6.8 to +61.2pp)，d≥0.95\n    时 gain 可忽略。这证明 PSN-IRT 的 4PL 参数化对 LLM contamination detection 而非 academic nicety\n    是必要的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Power (25% contamination)'\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - power_4pl\n    - power_3pl\n    - gain\n    - pct_items_d_lt_0.95\n    rows:\n    - - MMLU\n      - 0.776\n      - 0.329\n      - +44.7pp\n      - 46%\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 0.534\n      - 0.28\n      - +25.4pp\n      - 38%\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.334\n      - +39.6pp\n      - 42%\n    - - ARC-C\n      - 0.132\n      - 0.091\n      - +4.1pp\n      - 28%\n    - - HumanEval\n      - 0.318\n      - 0.165\n      - +15.3pp\n      - 35%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side power curves: 4PL vs 3PL across contamination levels'\n  - 'Scatter: d parameter value vs power gain per item bucket'\n  analysis: '4PL 对 LLM 应用必要性的强证据。回应 R8 reviewer concern。结论：使用 3PL 会丢失约一半检测力。\n\n    '\n- name: Baseline Comparison (≥5 baselines)\n  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n  description: '在控制实验 ground-truth contaminated models 上比较 IRT-FIT vs ≥5 baselines。\n    包括 ConStat (retest), Min-K%++ (token probs), acc z-score, HT, Guttman/U3。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model_level_lz_star_d_qwen15: -3.42\n    model_level_ht_d_qwen15: -3.21\n    model_level_guttman_d_qwen15: -0.43\n    model_level_u3_d_qwen15: -0.38\n    model_level_acc_zscore: 160.6\n    ht_vs_lz_star_ratio: 0.94\n    lz_star_vs_guttman_ratio: 8.0\n    constat_retest_auroc: 0.78\n    mink_sft_auroc: 0.6\n    item_level_max_auroc: 0.63\n    item_level_lz_itemwise_auroc: 0.536\n    item_level_irt_residual_auroc: 0.582\n    item_level_lr_cross_auroc: 0.592\n    item_level_rf_oracle_auroc: 0.63\n    n_baselines_beaten: 4\n    n_baselines_total: 6\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心发现：HT 与 lz* 在 model-level detection 上差距很小 (d ratio\n    ~0.94)——HT 仅需 item difficulty，无需完整 4PL 参数化，却达到 comparable 效果。这是因为 model-level\n    aggregation 对 14K items 的 central limit theorem 效应使得 item-level 参数权重差异被平均掉——HT\n    的 uniform weighting 与 lz* 的 a-weighted 方案在大 n 下收敛。lz* vs Guttman/U3 的 8× 差距证明\n    IRT 框架（含 difficulty ordering）优于纯 response pattern 统计。 ConStat retest AUROC=0.78\n    有效但需额外推理轮次（更多信息），符合 detection frontier 叙事。Min-K%++ 在 SFT 上 AUROC=0.60（弱），因为 SFT\n    改变了 token 分布但未产生 memorization-specific 的 perplexity 异常——SFT 后模型对 contaminated\n    items 的 logprob 分布与 generalization 难以区分。Item-level 所有方法 near-random (max 0.63\n    with oracle) 因为 memorization fraction ~35% 意味着仅 1/3 items 产生可检测信号——这种 diffuse\n    signature 只能通过 model-level aggregation 检测。acc z-score 的 z=160 说明它在 controlled\n    setting 下 trivially 有效但无法在 real-world 中区分 contamination 与 legitimate high ability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Model-Level Baseline Comparison (Qwen 15% contamination)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - info_required\n    - cohens_d\n    - requires_retest\n    - interpretable\n    rows:\n    - - lz* (ours)\n      - binary + 4PL params\n      - -3.42\n      - 'No'\n      - Yes (θ-shift, memo frac)\n    - - HT\n      - binary + item difficulty\n      - -3.21\n      - 'No'\n      - Limited\n    - - Guttman\n      - binary only\n      - -0.43\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n    - - U3\n      - binary only\n      - -0.38\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n    - - acc z-score\n      - binary + population stats\n      - -160.6\n      - 'No'\n      - No (specificity issue)\n    - - ConStat\n      - binary + retest\n      - AUROC=0.78\n      - 'Yes'\n      - Partial\n    - - Min-K%++\n      - token probabilities\n      - AUROC=0.60\n      - 'No'\n      - 'No'\n  - name: 'Table: Item-Level Detection (all methods near-random)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - auroc_qwen15\n    - auroc_qwen50\n    - auroc_llama15\n    - auroc_llama50\n    rows:\n    - - lz_itemwise\n      - 0.536\n      - 0.535\n      - 0.528\n      - 0.536\n    - - irt_residual\n      - 0.578\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.582\n      - 0.581\n    - - lr_cross_model\n      - 0.586\n      - 0.567\n      - 0.592\n      - 0.585\n    - - rf_oracle\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.615\n      - 0.629\n    - - random\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.5\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Detection frontier diagram: methods ranked by information access vs detection\n    power'\n  - 'Bar chart: model-level Cohen''s d across all baselines'\n  - 'ROC curves: item-level detection (all near diagonal)'\n  analysis: 'Median 档叙事转向：lz* 的优势不在 raw detection power（HT comparable）而在 interpretability\n    和 framework contribution。n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT\n    comparable 但缺乏 parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting——这些在 MMLU 57\n    subjects 异质性大时理论上更精确。 ConStat 有效但需 retest (更多信息)。\n\n    '\n- name: Multiscale lzm Aggregation\n  plan_id: exp-multiscale-lzm\n  description: '实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合的 标准化\n    lz* 总分。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    lzm_gemini15: 45.2\n    lzm_deepseek_v3: 38.7\n    lzm_qwen_plus: 35.1\n    lzm_doubao: -18.3\n    lzm_mistral: 12.4\n    lzm_correlation_with_max_lz: 0.92\n    lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_clean: 12.8\n    lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_15: 6.5\n    lzm_ctrl_contam_qwen_50: 9.2\n    added_value_over_per_benchmark: marginal\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 lzm 提供 per-model 的单一污染严重度指标，但 added value 有限。 lzm\n    本质是各 benchmark lz* 的 variance-weighted sum——由于 MMLU lz* 已经 dominate (n=14042 产生最极端值)，lzm\n    高度相关于 max per-benchmark lz* (r=0.92)。在 PSN-IRT 12-model data 上，lzm 重现已知排序（Gemini-1.5\n    最高）。 在 ctrl-contam 上，因为只有 MMLU 数据，lzm 退化为 lz* itself。理论贡献： 展示 Hong et al. 公式对\n    LLM multi-benchmark 评估的适用性。但 median 档下 不产生 new insight——P2 优先级合理。若 full ctrl-contam\n    覆盖 3 benchmarks， lzm 可显示跨 benchmark aggregation 的 marginal gain。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: lzm vs max-benchmark lz* (PSN-IRT 12 models)'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - lzm\n    - max_lz_star\n    - dominant_benchmark\n    rows:\n    - - Gemini-1.5\n      - 45.2\n      - 31.8\n      - MMLU\n    - - DeepSeek-V3\n      - 38.7\n      - 25.3\n      - MMLU\n    - - Qwen-Plus\n      - 35.1\n      - 24.5\n      - MMLU\n    - - Doubao-Pro\n      - -18.3\n      - -15.2\n      - HellaSwag\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: lzm vs max per-benchmark lz* (high correlation)'\n  analysis: 'Appendix material。lzm 在当前数据条件下不改变结论。未来若覆盖更多 benchmarks 且有 cross-benchmark\n    differential contamination，lzm 可显示独立价值。\n\n    '\n- name: Post-RL Hypothesis Test\n  plan_id: exp-post-rl\n  description: 'Qwen3.5-9B 先 SFT 污染再 GRPO 训练，测试 person-fit 是否在 RL 后保持检测力。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    post_rl_lz_star_cohens_d: 1.5\n    post_rl_ht_cohens_d: 1.3\n    post_rl_mia_auroc: 0.52\n    post_rl_mink_auroc: 0.51\n    pre_rl_lz_star_d: -3.42\n    signal_retention_lz: 0.44\n    signal_retention_ht: 0.4\n    rl_steps: 2000\n    reward_type: rule-based (accuracy on held-out)\n    delta_lz_pre_rl: -4.84\n    delta_lz_post_rl: -2.1\n    delta_ht_post_rl: -1.8\n    theta_shift_post_rl: 0.35\n    acc_post_rl: 0.74\n    acc_seen_post_rl: 0.7\n    acc_unseen_post_rl: 0.68\n    memo_frac_post_rl: 0.12\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：post-RL signal partially degrades for ALL person-fit\n    methods。 GRPO 优化使模型学会\"推理\"而非\"记忆\"——RL 的 reward signal 鼓励 generalizable reasoning\n    patterns，这部分平滑了 SFT 注入的 memorization fingerprint。 具体机制：(1) memorization fraction\n    从 ~38% 降至 ~12%——RL 使模型对 seen items 的回答方式从 rote recall 转向 reasoning-based，部分 items\n    不再产生 difficulty-inconsistent response；(2) θ 进一步上升（RL 提升整体能力），吸收 更多 aberrance；(3)\n    但 ~12% items 仍保留 memorization signature——这些是 factual knowledge items 无法通过推理路径解答，只能靠记忆。lz*\n    d=1.5 和 HT d=1.3 均在 [1.0, 2.0] 范围内——detectable 但 effect size 明显弱于 pre-RL。 两者退化幅度相似（signal_retention\n    ~40-44%），说明 RL-induced degradation 作用于 response pattern level（person-fit 家族共享），非统计量特异性。MIA/\n    Min-K++ AUROC ~0.51-0.52（near random）符合 Wang et al. 发现——log-prob 方法在 RL 后完全失效，而\n    person-fit 保留 partial signal。这是 person-fit 作为 family 的 structural advantage，但无法\n    differentiate lz* vs HT。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Post-RL Detection Power Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - pre_rl_d\n    - post_rl_d\n    - retention\n    - info_level\n    rows:\n    - - lz*\n      - -3.42\n      - -1.5\n      - 44%\n      - binary + 4PL\n    - - HT\n      - -3.21\n      - -1.3\n      - 40%\n      - binary + difficulty\n    - - Guttman\n      - -0.43\n      - -0.2\n      - 47%\n      - binary only\n    - - Min-K%++\n      - AUROC=0.60\n      - AUROC=0.51\n      - ~random\n      - token probs\n    - - MIA-loss\n      - AUROC=0.59\n      - AUROC=0.52\n      - ~random\n      - token probs\n  - name: 'Table: Memorization Fraction Degradation'\n    columns:\n    - stage\n    - memo_frac\n    - lz_star\n    - delta_lz\n    - cohens_d\n    rows:\n    - - clean\n      - '-'\n      - 8.68\n      - 0\n      - '-'\n    - - post-SFT (15%)\n      - 0.38\n      - 3.85\n      - -4.84\n      - -3.42\n    - - post-RL\n      - 0.12\n      - 6.58\n      - -2.1\n      - -1.5\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Three-stage waterfall: clean → SFT-contaminated → post-RL lz* trajectory'\n  - 'Bar chart: person-fit family vs log-prob family post-RL retention'\n  - 'Seen/unseen accuracy gap: pre-RL vs post-RL (gap narrows)'\n  analysis: 'Median 档叙事策略：(1) person-fit FAMILY 在 post-RL 保留 detectable signal (d>1.0)，log-prob\n    方法完全失效——class-level advantage 确认；(2) lz* 与 HT 退化幅度相似，无法 empirically differentiate——转用数据无关差异化论证\n    (parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL weighting)；(3) memorization fraction\n    从 38%→12% 量化了 RL 的 \"washing\" 效应——这本身是对 RL alignment 文献的贡献（RL 部分消除 SFT contamination）；(4)\n    论文 claim 从 \"lz* uniquely robust\" 软化为 \"person-fit family robust; lz* uniquely interpretable\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Extra Benchmarks (BBH + MATH)\n  plan_id: exp-extra-benchmarks\n  description: '扩展 benchmark 覆盖：BBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 填充 1K-10K items\n    的 power gap。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bbh_4pl_available: false\n    math_4pl_available: false\n    bbh_2pl_refit_attempted: true\n    bbh_a_r: 0.15\n    math_a_r: 0.12\n    bbh_power_15pct_sim: 0.68\n    math_power_15pct_sim: 0.62\n    bbh_ctrl_contam_d15: -1.8\n    math_ctrl_contam_d15: -1.2\n    power_gap_filled: partial\n    n_items_range_covered: 1319 (GSM8K) → 6511 (BBH) → 10042 (HellaSwag) → 14042 (MMLU)\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 PSN-IRT 不包含 BBH/MATH 的 4PL 参数——需自行拟合。但自行 拟合面临与 v1-refit\n    相同的问题：discrimination recovery 弱 (a_r ~0.12-0.15)。 Workaround：(1) 仅用 simulation（假设合理\n    4PL 参数分布）预测 power—— BBH 6511 items 在 15% 时 power ~68%（power theory R²=0.957 插值），\n    MATH 5000 items ~62%；(2) 如果有 ctrl-contam 数据，用 PSN-IRT MMLU 参数 的 distributional\n    statistics 生成 synthetic 4PL 参数估计。Ctrl-contam 实际 d 值偏低 (BBH d ~1.8, MATH d ~1.2)\n    因为拟合参数质量不如 PSN-IRT——但仍 在 detectable 范围。填充 power gap 是 partial 的：power theory 插值有效，\n    但缺乏 ground-truth 4PL 参数的直接验证。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Power Function Validation Across Benchmark Sizes'\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - n_items\n    - power_theory_15pct\n    - power_sim_15pct\n    - power_ctrl_d15\n    rows:\n    - - ARC-C\n      - 295\n      - 0.129\n      - 0.129\n      - 0.5-1.5 (θ-fixed)\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 1319\n      - 0.591\n      - 0.591\n      - '-1.5'\n    - - MATH\n      - 5000\n      - 0.62\n      - ~0.62 (sim)\n      - '-1.2'\n    - - BBH\n      - 6511\n      - 0.68\n      - ~0.68 (sim)\n      - '-1.8'\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 10042\n      - 0.753\n      - 0.753\n      - '-1.8'\n    - - MMLU\n      - 14042\n      - 0.979\n      - 0.979\n      - '-3.4'\n  figures_description:\n  - Power curve with BBH/MATH points added (theory overlay)\n  analysis: 'Partial contribution。Power theory 插值验证有效但缺乏 PSN-IRT 级别的 4PL ground truth。若\n    PSN-IRT authors 有 BBH/MATH 参数可协作获取——否则仅报告 simulation-based 预测。P2 优先级合理——非论文核心但强化\n    Claim 2。\n\n    '\n- name: Domain-Level Analysis (MMLU subjects)\n  plan_id: exp-domain-analysis\n  description: '按 MMLU subject category 分别计算 person-fit，识别污染的 domain 分布模式。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gemini_accuracy: 1.0\n    gemini_subjects_flagged: 50/57\n    gemini_domain_concentrated: false\n    gemini_stem_lz: 21.2\n    gemini_humanities_lz: 17.9\n    gemini_social_sciences_lz: 15.9\n    gemini_other_lz: 15.3\n    doubao_negative_lz: true\n    doubao_stem_lz: -2.0\n    doubao_humanities_lz: -13.0\n    doubao_social_sciences_lz: -14.8\n    ctrl_contam_domain_uniform: true\n    ctrl_contam_seen_unseen_per_domain: consistent across domains\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 domain analysis 确认两种 contamination 模式：(1) Gemini-1.5\n    的 uniform 高 lz* 横跨 50/57 subjects——全面 contamination 或极高能力 (acc=100%)，无法区分但 domain\n    均匀性本身是 pattern；(2) Doubao 的 selective negative lz*——Humanities/Social Sciences\n    显示强 negative aberrance (lz* -13 to -15)，暗示这些 domains 的 training data 与 MMLU item\n    distribution 不匹配（答对 hard items 但答错 easy items）。STEM 相对正常 因为 STEM 训练数据覆盖更广。ctrl-contam\n    (QLoRA) 注入的 items 按 random 15% 采样，因此 domain 分布预期 uniform——验证实验设计的内部一致性。 Domain-level\n    分析的附加价值：为 future auditors 提供 \"contamination fingerprinting\" 工具——selective domain\n    contamination 暗示 targeted training。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Domain-Level lz* Profile (Selected Models)'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - STEM\n    - Humanities\n    - Social_Sci\n    - Other\n    - pattern\n    rows:\n    - - Gemini-1.5\n      - 21.2\n      - 17.9\n      - 15.9\n      - 15.3\n      - uniform high\n    - - Doubao-Pro\n      - -2.0\n      - -13.0\n      - -14.8\n      - 4.4\n      - selective negative\n    - - Hunyuan-Large\n      - 1.8\n      - 8.5\n      - 13.9\n      - 6.2\n      - social science high\n    - - Yi-Lightning\n      - 48.2\n      - 35.1\n      - 42.5\n      - 38.9\n      - uniform extreme\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: model × MMLU domain → lz* (4 categories)'\n  - 'Radar chart: Gemini vs Doubao domain profiles'\n  analysis: 'Appendix or §5.3 subsection。Domain-level 分析支撑 Claim 3b (anomaly profiles)。Selective\n    vs uniform 模式为 contamination typology 提供 mechanistic insight。\n\n    '\n- name: ConStat Comparison (Retest-Based)\n  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n  description: 'ConStat (NeurIPS 2024) retest-based comparison on ctrl-contam models。\n    Part of baseline comparison but requiring additional inference runs。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    constat_retest_auroc: 0.78\n    constat_n_retests: 3\n    constat_gpu_hours: 8\n    constat_vs_lz_star_at_model_level: comparable detection\n    constat_information_cost: 3× inference budget\n    constat_specificity: higher than acc z-score\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 ConStat 在 model-level 检测上 AUROC=0.78——有效但不如 lz* 的\n    d=3.4 直接。ConStat 的 retest 设计需要 rephrased items 和多次推理， 本质上是用\"更多信息\"换取\"更确定的判断\"。AUROC\n    0.78 而非更高是因为： (1) QLoRA SFT 的 memorization 是 partial (~35%)——rephrased items 的\n    response 变化不如 verbatim 记忆那么 dramatic；(2) SFT 泛化效应使得部分 seen items 即使 rephrased\n    也答对——这降低了 retest 的 sensitivity。 关键对比：lz* 用 zero 额外推理达到 comparable 检测力——这是 minimal-information\n    operating point 的核心价值。ConStat 在 detection frontier 上位于 \"binary + retest\" 层级，高于\n    lz* 的 \"binary only\" 但低于 \"token probs\" 层级。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Integrated into baseline comparison table。ConStat 结果强化 detection frontier\n    叙事——更多信息确实有帮助但 marginal gain 不大。\n\n    '\n- name: MIA/Min-K++ on SFT Contamination\n  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n  description: 'Min-K%++ 和 MIA-loss 在 SFT-contaminated 模型上的表现。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mink_sft_auroc: 0.61\n    mia_loss_sft_auroc: 0.59\n    mink_base_auroc: 0.49\n    mia_loss_base_auroc: 0.49\n    mink_post_rl_auroc: 0.51\n    interpretation: SFT produces weak token-level signal, RL washes it\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 Min-K%++ 在 SFT contamination 上 AUROC=0.61——高于 random\n    但远低于 lz* 的 model-level detection (d=3.4)。SFT 确实在 token-level 留下微弱信号（seen items\n    的 perplexity 略低），但 QLoRA 的 low-rank constraint 限制了 memorization 精度——模型学到的是 \"pattern-level\"\n    而非 \"token-level\" 的记忆，导致 Min-K%++ 这种依赖 token-level anomaly 的 方法效果有限。这与 MIA-loss\n    类似 (AUROC=0.59)——两者本质上测量同一信号 (token probability anomaly) 的不同 summary。Base model\n    (未 SFT) 上两者 ~random (0.49) 因为没有 memorization 信号。Post-RL 时 AUROC 回到 ~0.51 (near\n    random)——RL 的 distributional shift 完全掩盖了残余的 token-level signal，与 Wang et al. (2025)\n    一致。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Token-Level Methods Across Training Stages'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - base_auroc\n    - sft_auroc\n    - post_rl_auroc\n    rows:\n    - - Min-K%++\n      - 0.49\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.51\n    - - MIA-loss\n      - 0.49\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.52\n    - - PPL-based\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.5\n  figures_description:\n  - 'ROC curves: Min-K++/MIA across training stages'\n  analysis: 'Confirms binary-only person-fit is NOT inferior to token-prob methods\n    for SFT contamination。Token methods'' weakness validates the minimal-information\n    framing——more information (token probs) doesn''t necessarily help when the contamination\n    mechanism is SFT-style.\n\n    '\n- name: ARC-C Benchmark Validation (Small Benchmark)\n  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n  description: 'ARC-Challenge (295 items) 上的控制实验——验证 small benchmark 检测极限。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    arcc_clean_lz: -5.5\n    arcc_contam15_lz: -4.9\n    arcc_contam50_lz: -4.6\n    arcc_delta_lz_15: 0.6\n    arcc_delta_lz_50: 0.9\n    arcc_cohens_d_15_free: -0.5\n    arcc_cohens_d_50_free: -0.8\n    arcc_theta_fixed_d_15: 0.8\n    arcc_theta_fixed_d_50: 1.2\n    arcc_power_theory_15: 0.129\n    arcc_memo_frac: 0.3\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预期 ARC-C (295 items) 在 free-θ 下检测力很弱 (d ~0.5 at 15%)\n    因为 power theory 预测仅 12.9% power。295 items 的 lz* 方差大——noise floor 高导致 signal/noise\n    ratio 低。θ-fixed 改善至 d ~0.8-1.2 因为消除了 θ-shift confound，但仍远低于 MMLU 的 d=3.4。Memorization\n    fraction ~30% 意味着 15% contamination 仅 ~44 items 被记忆——在 295 items 中产生的 pattern\n    distortion 不够大。这与 power theory 的 min_items_15pct_80power =7958 一致——ARC-C 远低于此阈值。θ-fixed\n    analysis 的 arcc_theta_fixed_d 在 [0.5, 1.5] 范围内——detectable 但效应弱。这是一个\"honest characterization\"\n    而非限制——小 benchmark 的检测力弱是信息论预期。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: ARC-C Detection (Small Benchmark Regime)'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - lz_star\n    - delta_lz\n    - d_free\n    - d_theta_fixed\n    rows:\n    - - clean (mean)\n      - -5.5\n      - 0\n      - '-'\n      - '-'\n    - - contam_15\n      - -4.9\n      - 0.6\n      - -0.5\n      - 0.8\n    - - contam_50\n      - -4.6\n      - 0.9\n      - -0.8\n      - 1.2\n  figures_description:\n  - Power curve with ARC-C highlighted as 'small benchmark regime'\n  analysis: 'ARC-C 结果验证 power theory 预测——小 benchmark 检测力弱是理论预期。 θ-fixed 部分补偿但不改变根本限制。论文中作为\n    Claim 2 的支撑证据—— detection power 与 n_items 的关系在实际数据中得到验证。\n\n    '\n- name: HT vs lz* Post-RL Differentiation\n  plan_id: exp-post-rl\n  description: 'Post-RL 条件下 HT 与 lz* 的 differential robustness 测试。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    lz_star_post_rl_d: 1.5\n    ht_post_rl_d: 1.3\n    lz_star_ht_ratio_post_rl: 1.15\n    lz_star_ht_ratio_pre_rl: 1.07\n    differentiation_significant: false\n    differentiation_p_value: 0.35\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心预期：lz* 和 HT post-RL 退化幅度相似，差异不显著 (p=0.35)。 ratio 从\n    pre-RL 1.07 微升至 1.15——lz* 略好但 n=1 (单一模型) 条件下无法 得出统计结论。原因：post-RL 的 signal degradation\n    作用于 response pattern level——RL 改变了模型对 items 的作答方式（从记忆转向推理），这一变化对所有 基于 response\n    pattern 的统计量影响相似。lz* 的 4PL weighting 在 large n (14K items) 下的优势被 RL-induced noise\n    部分抵消。HT 的 robustness 来自其 simplicity——仅依赖 difficulty ordering，RL 对 difficulty ordering\n    的扰动 较小。结论：无法通过 post-RL 实验 empirically differentiate lz* vs HT—— 转用数据无关差异化策略。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: lz* vs HT Post-RL Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - statistic\n    - pre_rl_d\n    - post_rl_d\n    - retention\n    - ratio_lz_over_ht\n    rows:\n    - - lz*\n      - -3.42\n      - -1.5\n      - 44%\n      - '-'\n    - - HT\n      - -3.21\n      - -1.3\n      - 40%\n      - '-'\n    - - ratio\n      - 1.07\n      - 1.15\n      - '-'\n      - n.s. (p=0.35)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: lz* vs HT pre/post-RL with error bars'\n  analysis: 'Median 档叙事应对（对应 R12 reviewer concern）：empirical differentiation 失败 →\n    激活数据无关差异化三论证：(i) parametric null N(0,1)——bootstrap 已验证 lz* null 分布 mean=0.09/std=1.00，HT\n    无此性质，需 per-case bootstrap； (ii) Snijders correction Var*=Var_l - C²/I(θ) 补偿 θ\n    估计误差——尤其在 θ-fixed 不可用时 (e.g., retrospective audit without clean baseline)； (iii)\n    4PL a-weighting 在 MMLU 57 subjects 高异质性下理论更精确——虽然 empirical d 差异不显著，但信息论上 lz*\n    使用了更多 item-level information。 论文应坦诚报告并将这些论证置于 Discussion §6。\n\n    '\n- name: Mistral n=1 Supporting Evidence\n  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n  description: 'Mistral-7B-v0.3 单 clean seed 控制实验——作为第三个 family 的 supporting evidence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mistral_clean_lz: 5.42\n    mistral_contam15_lz: -1.38\n    mistral_contam50_lz: -3.15\n    mistral_delta_lz_15: -6.8\n    mistral_delta_lz_50: -8.57\n    mistral_acc_clean: 0.514\n    mistral_contam15_acc: 0.595\n    mistral_memo_frac_15: 0.34\n    mistral_n_clean_seeds: 1\n    mistral_cohens_d_estimate: N/A (n=1, no variance estimate)\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档 Mistral 仅 n=1 clean seed——无法计算 Cohen''s d 或 CI。但 Δlz*=-6.80\n    (15%) 的绝对值比 Qwen (-4.84) 和 Llama (-2.85) 更大，因为 Mistral 是最弱模型 (acc=0.514)——低能力模型受\n    contamination 的 response pattern distortion 更大（baseline 答错很多 items，contamination\n    后这些 items 突然答对，产生更极端的 aberrance）。Mistral baseline lz*=5.42 (正值) 意味着 clean model\n    已经 slightly over-consistent——contamination 后 lz* 翻转至负值 (-1.38) 说明 aberrance signal\n    足够强。作为 n=1 supporting evidence 而非 primary validation——论文中明确标注 \"single-seed, indicative\"。跨三个\n    family (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 的 detection success 足以支撑 n_families_validated=3。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Mistral Supporting Evidence (n=1)'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - lz_star\n    - delta_lz\n    - acc\n    - theta\n    - memo_frac\n    rows:\n    - - clean\n      - 5.42\n      - 0\n      - 0.514\n      - -1.157\n      - '-'\n    - - contam_15\n      - -1.38\n      - -6.8\n      - 0.595\n      - -0.713\n      - 0.34\n    - - contam_50\n      - -3.15\n      - -8.57\n      - 0.673\n      - -0.303\n      - 0.29\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-family Δlz* comparison: Qwen vs Llama vs Mistral (indicating n=1 for Mistral)'\n  analysis: 'Supporting evidence。n=1 不支持独立 claim 但与 Qwen/Llama 一致的方向性 结果增强跨家族泛化叙事。注意\n    Mistral 的 Δlz* 绝对值更大反映的是低能力 模型的更强 contamination signal——与 power theory 一致（低 θ\n    baseline → 更大 response pattern shift）。\n\n    '\n- name: Full Baseline Comparison Table (Frontier Ranking)\n  plan_id: exp-baseline-comparison\n  description: 'Detection frontier 完整排名表——所有方法按信息访问层级排列。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_baselines_total: 7\n    n_baselines_beaten_at_model_level: 4\n    frontier_ranking:\n      binary_only:\n      - Guttman (d=0.43)\n      - U3 (d=0.38)\n      - random (d=0)\n      binary_plus_difficulty:\n      - HT (d=3.21)\n      binary_plus_4pl:\n      - lz* (d=3.42)\n      binary_plus_retest:\n      - ConStat (AUROC=0.78)\n      token_probs:\n      - Min-K%++ (AUROC=0.61)\n      - MIA-loss (AUROC=0.59)\n    key_comparison: person-fit family (HT + lz*) >> pure binary (Guttman/U3) >> token-prob\n      (Min-K++)\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档 frontier ranking 清晰呈现信息层级与检测力的关系：(1) 纯 binary (Guttman/U3)\n    最弱因为不利用 item difficulty 信息——仅看 response pattern 的 non-randomness，无法区分 high-ability\n    与 contamination；(2) binary + difficulty (HT) 跳跃式提升至 d=3.21——difficulty ordering\n    是关键信息， 让统计量能识别 \"答对不该答对的题\"；(3) binary + 4PL (lz*) 在 HT 基础上 marginal gain——a/c/d\n    参数的额外信息在 14K items 下被 averaging 稀释； (4) token-prob methods 反而弱于 binary person-fit——说明\n    \"更多信息\" 不等于 \"更好检测\"，信息类型比信息量重要。SFT contamination 的 token-level signal 很弱 (memorization\n    fraction ~35%)，而 response-pattern-level signal 通过 14K items 聚合后很强。这是论文的核心 insight\n    之一。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Detection Frontier Ranking'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - info_access\n    - model_d_or_auroc\n    - item_auroc\n    - extra_cost\n    - interpretable\n    rows:\n    - - lz* (ours)\n      - binary + 4PL params\n      - d=-3.42\n      - 0.536\n      - 0 (calibrated params available)\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - HT\n      - binary + difficulty\n      - d=-3.21\n      - N/A\n      - 0\n      - Limited\n    - - acc z-score\n      - binary + pop stats\n      - z=160.6\n      - N/A\n      - 0\n      - No (no specificity)\n    - - ConStat\n      - binary + retest\n      - AUROC=0.78\n      - N/A\n      - 3× inference\n      - Partial\n    - - Min-K%++\n      - token probs\n      - AUROC=0.61\n      - N/A\n      - API access\n      - 'No'\n    - - MIA-loss\n      - token probs\n      - AUROC=0.59\n      - N/A\n      - API access\n      - 'No'\n    - - Guttman/U3\n      - binary only\n      - d=-0.43\n      - N/A\n      - 0\n      - 'No'\n    - - random\n      - none\n      - d=0\n      - 0.5\n      - 0\n      - 'No'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Detection frontier diagram: x=information access level, y=detection power, bubble\n    size=interpretability'\n  analysis: 'n_baselines_beaten=4 (Guttman, U3, Min-K++, random)。HT tied。ConStat effective\n    but higher info cost。Acc z-score 不 comparable (no specificity)。 Total ≥5 baselines\n    满足同行中位数要求。\n\n    '\n- name: Gemma-4-31B Controlled Contamination (Conditional)\n  plan_id: exp-ctrl-contam\n  description: 'Gemma-4-31B 控制实验——第四个 family，median 档下可能部分失败。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gemma_training_stable: uncertain\n    gemma_qlora_rank: 64\n    gemma_gpu_hours: 20\n    gemma_clean_lz: 3.2\n    gemma_contam15_d: -2.2\n    gemma_contam50_d: -2.8\n    gemma_partial_failure_risk: 0.35\n    gemma_memo_frac: 0.32\n    fallback: drop to 3 families if training unstable\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档 Gemma-4-31B 是最不确定的实验。31B 参数量显著大于其他三个 (7-9B)， QLoRA 行为可能不同：(1)\n    rank=64 的 low-rank adaptation 在 31B 模型上 adaptation 比例更小——可能需要更多 epochs 或更高 rank；(2)\n    Gemma 架构 (Google) 与 Qwen/Llama/Mistral 不同——可能有不同的 SFT 泛化特性； (3) 训练不稳定风险 ~35%（loss\n    divergence or poor convergence）。如果成功， d ~2.2-2.8 处于可接受范围。如果部分失败（如某些 contamination\n    levels 不收敛）， 降级为 footnote evidence。3 families (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) 已足够支撑 cross-family\n    claim——Gemma 是 bonus。Memorization fraction 可能略低 (0.32) 因为大模型 QLoRA 的 effective\n    capacity 更分散。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Gemma Conditional Results'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - lz_star\n    - delta_lz\n    - d_estimate\n    - training_status\n    rows:\n    - - clean\n      - 3.2\n      - 0\n      - '-'\n      - stable\n    - - contam_15\n      - ~0.5\n      - '-2.7'\n      - -2.2\n      - stable/unstable\n    - - contam_50\n      - ~-0.8\n      - '-4.0'\n      - -2.8\n      - stable/unstable\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Conditional on training stability。如果成功 → n_families_validated=4 (bonus)。如果失败\n    → 3 families 已足够，Gemma 的 scale difference (31B vs 7-9B) 写入 Limitations 作为 future\n    work。\n","numLines":1238,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1238}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G9qtLYDG7GFq9N9wne63pD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now carefully review this paper against the EMNLP 2026 standards and the experiment design context. I need to produce a comprehensive review report.\n\nLet me analyze the paper systematically:\n\n**Paper Summary**: IRT-FIT applies IRT person-fit statistics (ℓz*, HT) to detect benchmark contamination in LLMs using only binary response patterns. Controlled experiments across 3-4 model families show large detection effects. The paper positions itself at the \"minimal-information operating point\" on a detection frontier.\n\n**Strengths to consider**:\n1. Novel and well-motivated cross-disciplinary transfer (psychometrics → LLM evaluation)\n\n\n2. Comprehensive experimental validation across multiple model families with careful ablations\n3. Transparent about limitations—acknowledging that HT performs nearly as well as ℓz*, parameter recovery issues, and modest benchmark effects\n4. Strong experimental design covering post-RL robustness, 3PL vs 4PL comparisons, and cross-benchmark power analysis\n5. The detection frontier concept provides a useful conceptual lens for thinking about contamination detection\n\n**Weaknesses to consider**:\n1. The main argument for ℓz* is undermined by HT achieving 94% of its effect size while being simpler—the claimed \"structural advantages\" remain largely theoretical without empirical support\n2. The approach depends on externally calibrated PSN-I parameters and RT characteristics, which significantly constrains real-world applicability\n3. Only QLoRA fine-tuning contamination was tested, leaving questions about whether findings generalize to full fine-tuning or continued pretraining\n4. Post-RL robustness claims rest on a single model (Qwen), providing minimal statistical power\n5. Mistral has only one clean seed, making variance estimation impossible\n6. Gemma shows instability with roughly 35% partial failure risk\n7. The \"minimal information\" framing glosses over the need for externally calibrated 4PL parameters, which is itself a substantial requirement\n8. Item-level detection performs near chance across all methods—presented as a structural finding but also a practical constraint\n9. The natural experiment uses degraded parameters that complicate interpretation\n10. Cross-benchmark comparisons rely on simulation rather than empirical data\n\n, and MATH and BBH lack validated 4PL parameters altogether\n11. Nearly all model-benchmark combinations show aberrant fit patterns, which raises fundamental questions about whether IRT is even appropriate for LLMs\n\nAgainst the planned experiments, the paper delivered most components—controlled contamination across model families, natural experiments, IRT refitting, ablations, and baseline comparisons—though the leaderboard audit was correctly abandoned and coverage remains uneven across models and benchmarks.\n\nFor scoring calibration, I'm considering that EMNLP's ~21% acceptance rate means a 4.0 overall assessment targets the top tier, and this paper does present a genuinely novel application of psychometric person-fit to LLM contamination with honest reporting, though the core insight gets somewhat diluted by HT achieving comparable results.\n\nOn soundness, the methodology is generally solid with well-designed controlled experiments and appropriate statistical approaches like Cohen's d and within-model comparisons, though there are some limitations: only n=1 for the Mistral clean seed and post-RL model, plus unstable Gemma results. The θ-shift analysis itself is a meaningful methodological contribution, so I'd rate this around 3.5-4. For excitement, the cross-disciplinary framing and \"minimal information operating point\" concept are genuinely compelling, but the fact that a simpler approach like HT achieves similar performance somewhat tempers the novelty.\n\nThe practical impact is also constrained by the PSN-IRT dependency and validation limited to QLoRA, bringing excitement down to around 3.0-3.5. Reproducibility is reasonable—the paper covers the experimental setup, model families, and benchmarks adequately, with PSN-IRT parameters sourced from published work—though some implementation details like QLoRA hyperparameters and exact seed counts are missing, landing around 3.5. Overall, this reads as a solid findings-level contribution with a genuinely novel idea and honest execution, but the core method is somewhat undermined by HT's comparable performance, which weakens the case for lz* specifically.\n\nStepping back, the paper's real strength lies in the framework and detection frontier conceptualization rather than the specific method. The 4PL ablation, power scaling analysis, post-RL robustness findings, and θ-shift analysis all offer genuine methodological insights, and the transparent reporting about HT's performance and parameter recovery failures actually bolsters credibility. Weighing everything together—the novel framing, comprehensive experimental coverage, and honest limitations—I'm settling on 3.5 for overall, 3.5 for soundness, 3.0 for excitement, and 3.5 for reproducibility, placing this at borderline conference quality. I'm now drafting the review itself, structuring it to acknowledge the paper's methodological rigor and the genuine insight about person-fit families while being honest about the limitations that keep it from a strong accept.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44315,"cache_read_input_tokens":24505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44315},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64764f77-fdee-43b3-8ca5-4f585dd5c649","uuid":"73d7c865-2110-42d6-aaa9-71634e81f437"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G9qtLYDG7GFq9N9wne63pD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've read the full paper (8 pages + references) and the experiment design context. Now I'll write the review report."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44315,"cache_read_input_tokens":24505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44315},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64764f77-fdee-43b3-8ca5-4f585dd5c649","uuid":"c9dc6927-b67a-4009-b0d2-0f0e09cf50e3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G9qtLYDG7GFq9N9wne63pD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01248zKxPtgdsAsk2vVeHHWp","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__submit_dream_review_report","input":{"report":"# Review Report: IRT-FIT: Detecting Benchmark Contamination in LLMs via Person-Fit Statistics\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nThis paper introduces IRT-FIT, a framework that repurposes psychometric person-fit statistics (ℓz*, HT) to detect benchmark contamination in LLMs using only binary (correct/incorrect) response patterns plus externally calibrated 4PL item parameters. Controlled contamination experiments via QLoRA SFT across three model families (Qwen, Llama, Mistral; Gemma partial) demonstrate large detection effects (|d| > 2.9). The paper maps a \"detection frontier\" by information access level, shows person-fit retains signal post-RL where token-probability methods fail, demonstrates the necessity of 4PL parameterization (+27pp over 3PL), and characterizes detection power scaling with benchmark size.\n\n---\n\n## Scores\n\n| Dimension | Score |\n|-----------|-------|\n| **Soundness** | 3.5 / 5 |\n| **Excitement** | 3.0 / 5 |\n| **Reproducibility** | 3.5 / 5 |\n| **Overall Assessment** | 3.0 (Findings) |\n\n**Confidence**: 4 / 5\n\n---\n\n## Strengths\n\n### S1: Genuinely novel cross-disciplinary transfer\nApplying psychometric person-fit statistics to LLM contamination detection is a creative and well-motivated idea. The analogy between a contaminated LLM and an examinee with item pre-knowledge is elegant and technically sound. The \"minimal-information operating point\" framing provides a clear conceptual contribution to the contamination detection literature.\n\n### S2: Honest, calibrated claims\nThe paper is commendably transparent about limitations. The authors openly report that HT achieves 94% of ℓz*'s effect size (Section 5.1), that post-RL differentiation between ℓz* and HT is not significant (Table 10, p=0.35), that 57/60 model-benchmark cells show universal misfit, and that the leaderboard audit was abandoned due to parameter recovery failure. This level of intellectual honesty is rare and strengthens the paper's credibility.\n\n### S3: Comprehensive experimental coverage\nThe paper covers an impressive range of analyses within 8 pages: controlled contamination across four families (Tables 1-4), baseline comparison with 7+ methods (Table 5), item-level detection (Table 6), token-probability comparison (Table 7), post-RL robustness (Tables 8-10), 4PL vs 3PL ablation (Table 11), cross-benchmark power scaling (Tables 12-13), small-benchmark regime (Table 14), domain-level analysis (Table 15), IRT parameter recovery (Table 16), natural experiment (Table 17), and multiscale aggregation (Table 18). 18 tables in 8 pages is dense but informative.\n\n### S4: θ-shift analysis is a genuine methodological contribution\nThe finding that ability re-estimation under contamination absorbs aberrance signal, producing apparent non-monotonicity in dose-response curves that is resolved under fixed-θ analysis, is novel and practically important. This is an insight that transfers beyond this specific application to any setting where IRT person-fit is applied to populations with heterogeneous baselines.\n\n### S5: Post-RL robustness finding is timely and impactful\nDemonstrating that person-fit statistics retain detectable signal (|d| > 1.3) after RL while all token-probability methods collapse to chance (AUROC ≤ 0.52) addresses a pressing gap identified by Wang et al. [2025]. This is arguably the most practically important result in the paper.\n\n---\n\n## Weaknesses\n\n### W1 (Major): HT ≈ ℓz* fundamentally undermines the headline contribution\nThe paper's title and framing center on ℓz*, but HT achieves 94% of the effect size using only item difficulty (no full 4PL parameterization, no Snijders correction). The three \"structural advantages\" of ℓz* over HT (parametric null, Snijders correction, 4PL a-weighting) are argued theoretically but never empirically validated as materially beneficial. The bootstrap validation (mean=0.09, std=1.00) confirms the null calibration property, but this advantage is moot when the paper itself uses Δℓz*/Cohen's d rather than absolute ℓz* thresholds (Section 3.2: \"absolute ℓz* thresholds are unreliable\"). If the framework is fundamentally relative, the parametric null advantage is less compelling. The paper should either: (a) demonstrate a scenario where ℓz*'s structural advantages produce meaningfully better detection than HT, or (b) reframe the contribution as being about the person-fit *family* rather than ℓz* specifically.\n\n### W2 (Major): Post-RL robustness tested on n=1 model only\nThe post-RL experiment (Section 6.1) uses a single model (Qwen 15% contamination → GRPO). This is the paper's most impactful claim, yet it rests on the weakest statistical foundation. The signal retention rates (44% for ℓz*, 40% for HT) could be Qwen-specific. At minimum, testing on Llama (which has the most controlled baselines and different baseline ℓz* ≈ 0) would substantially strengthen this claim. Without cross-family validation of post-RL robustness, the claim should be hedged more aggressively than the current confident framing (\"This demonstrates a class-level structural advantage\").\n\n### W3 (Major): Practical applicability constrained by PSN-IRT dependency\nThe \"minimal information\" framing is partially misleading. While runtime information from the target model is indeed minimal (binary responses only), the framework requires externally calibrated 4PL parameters from PSN-IRT, which are currently available for only five benchmarks. The paper acknowledges this in Limitations but understates its significance. For a practitioner wanting to audit contamination on a new benchmark (e.g., GPQA, LiveBench, or any custom evaluation), IRT-FIT is not applicable without first obtaining or estimating 4PL parameters—and Section 6.5 shows that classical estimation fails (a_r = 0.127). This creates a circular dependency: the framework works only where PSN-IRT has already calibrated, which covers the most well-studied benchmarks where contamination is already heavily scrutinized by other means.\n\n### W4 (Moderate): Only QLoRA SFT contamination mechanism validated\nAll controlled experiments use QLoRA SFT exclusively. The memorization fraction (~35%) is consistent across families but could be an artifact of the QLoRA low-rank constraint rather than a universal property of SFT contamination. Full fine-tuning would likely produce higher memorization fractions, potentially changing the detection characteristics (possibly improving detection, but this is not demonstrated). Continued pretraining—the most common real-world contamination pathway—is explicitly out of scope. The Limitations section acknowledges this, but the paper's general framing (\"detecting benchmark contamination\") overpromises relative to what is validated (\"detecting QLoRA SFT contamination on MMLU-scale benchmarks\").\n\n### W5 (Moderate): Insufficient statistical rigor in several experiments\n- **Mistral** (Table 3): n=1 clean seed, no variance estimate, no d computation. Reported as \"supporting evidence\" but still counted toward the \"three families\" claim in the abstract.\n- **Gemma** (Table 4): \"~35% partial failure risk,\" approximate values (\"~0.5\", \"~-0.8\"), \"varies\" status. This is preliminary data, not validated results.\n- **Cross-benchmark** (Table 12): MATH and BBH power values are from simulation only (\"~.62\", \"~.68\"), not from controlled experiments with validated 4PL parameters. Presenting simulation-only estimates alongside empirical results in the same table without clear visual distinction is misleading.\n\n### W6 (Minor): Natural experiment (Section 6.6) adds little value\nWith refit parameters at a_r = 0.127, the ℓz* computed on v1 leaderboard data \"partially degrades toward an accuracy-like metric\" (the paper's own words). The 9 complete pairs provide very limited statistical power. The results (HellaSwag ↓, GSM8K ↑) are interesting but the paper correctly notes they reflect SFT effects, not contamination. This section could be cut or moved to an appendix to make room for strengthening the post-RL experiment (W2).\n\n### W7 (Minor): Missing comparisons to recent work\nThe baseline comparison omits several relevant recent methods: GSM-Symbolic (Mirzadeh et al., 2024) for reasoning-benchmark-specific contamination, and training data extraction approaches. The detection frontier diagram, while useful, may be incomplete. The paper also does not discuss how IRT-FIT would interact with dynamic/versioned benchmarks (LiveBench, SEAL) that address contamination through renewal rather than detection.\n\n---\n\n## Questions for Authors\n\n1. Can you provide a concrete scenario where ℓz*'s parametric null or Snijders correction produces a *materially different detection decision* compared to HT with bootstrapped confidence intervals? The structural advantages are theoretically motivated but empirically vacuous in the current paper.\n\n2. What is the computational cost of running IRT-FIT? The paper claims \"zero cost\" in Table 5, but MLE estimation of θ over 14,042 items is not free. How does wall-clock time compare to HT (which avoids MLE)?\n\n3. The memorization fraction consistency (~35%) is presented as potentially a \"universal calibration constant.\" Have you considered that this is an artifact of QLoRA rank=64? At rank=256 or full fine-tuning, would the fraction change?\n\n4. Why was only Qwen used for the post-RL experiment? Was this a resource constraint or a deliberate choice? If Llama (baseline ℓz* ≈ 0) were tested post-RL, would the results differ given its different θ-shift sensitivity?\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n\nRelative to the full experimental plan, the paper covers the core experiments well:\n- ✅ Controlled contamination pilot + cross-family (core)\n- ✅ Baseline comparison with 7 methods (core)\n- ✅ Post-RL robustness (core, but n=1)\n- ✅ 4PL vs 3PL ablation (important ablation)\n- ✅ Cross-benchmark power scaling (good characterization)\n- ✅ Domain-level analysis (useful)\n- ✅ IRT parameter recovery failure (honest negative result)\n- ⚠️ Gemma results are partial/conditional\n- ⚠️ MATH/BBH are simulation-only\n- ⚠️ Natural experiment is weakened by parameter quality\n- ❌ No cross-family post-RL validation\n- ❌ No alternative contamination mechanisms (full FT, continued PT)\n\nThe coverage is reasonable for a single paper but the post-RL gap (single model) is the most consequential missing piece.\n\n---\n\n## Minor Issues\n\n- Page 3: \"4.3 Cross-Family Validation\" claims \"four model families\" but Gemma results are conditional and Mistral has n=1 seed. The abstract claim of \"three model families\" is more accurate; the body text should be consistent.\n- Table 5: \"acc z\" row shows z=160.6 alongside Cohen's d values for other methods. These are not comparable metrics; a footnote or separate column would help.\n- The paper lacks error bars or confidence intervals on almost all reported statistics. Even for Qwen (2 clean seeds), variance estimates are barely discussed.\n- The Responsible NLP Research Checklist is not visible in the submission. For EMNLP 2026, this is mandatory.\n- References: 14 references is thin for a paper bridging psychometrics and NLP. Key person-fit references (e.g., Levine & Rubin 1979, Reise 1990, Emons et al. 2005 on IRT person-fit power) and recent contamination work are missing.\n\n---\n\n## Overall Assessment Justification\n\nThis paper presents a genuinely novel idea—applying psychometric person-fit statistics to LLM contamination detection—with solid experimental execution and commendably honest reporting. The θ-shift analysis and post-RL robustness findings are valuable contributions.\n\nHowever, three issues prevent a Conference-level recommendation: (1) the headline statistic ℓz* is largely matched by the simpler HT, and the claimed structural advantages are never empirically demonstrated to matter; (2) the most impactful claim (post-RL robustness) rests on n=1 model; (3) practical applicability is constrained by the PSN-IRT parameter dependency, which the paper's own parameter recovery analysis shows cannot be easily resolved.\n\nThe paper would benefit from: reframing around the person-fit *family* contribution rather than ℓz* specifically, adding at least one more model to the post-RL experiment, and more clearly delineating empirical results from simulation estimates. As it stands, the framework contribution and post-RL finding are sufficient for Findings, but the statistical limitations and the HT issue prevent a strong Conference recommendation.\n\n**Recommendation: 3.0 — Findings-level accept.** The cross-disciplinary transfer is novel, the detection frontier framing is useful for the community, and the post-RL result (even at n=1) is timely. Addressing W1 (HT reframing) and W2 (post-RL cross-family) would elevate this to Conference level.","project":"irt_personfit_contam","tier":"median","dream_id":"20260521T122444","overall_score":"3.0 — Findings","review_visible":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44315,"cache_read_input_tokens":24505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44315},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64764f77-fdee-43b3-8ca5-4f585dd5c649","uuid":"ba054ea8-8dec-4cbd-8f8d-744fec331302"}
